e Simulations tab to \"Why it happens\" and lead it with \"Why\nfractional logs become uniform\": products become sums (told through a\ncity growing by a percentage each decade) and a wide spread makes\nfractional logs nearly uniform (the density-stacking animation), both\nopen, with the formal math collapsed and the wide-range caveat visible.\nThese sections move here from \"How it works\".\n\nRecast the add-vs-multiply comparison as a town-growth exercise with\nduration presets only: each kind of growth shows its first-digit\ndistribution against Benford, a verdict and its population range.\nSliders, Play, RMSE readouts and the extra charts are removed. Quiz\nreview links point to the renamed tab.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ee0ccfc350524ffe06a49733c9561edbac38caa8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/govindgnair23/benford-distribution/git/trees/ee0ccfc350524ffe06a49733c9561edbac38caa8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/govindgnair23/benford-distribution/git/commits/f914714d2485714ee2a7781ab6f127e491ccb690","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7546100?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/govindgnair23/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/govindgnair23/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/govindgnair23/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/govindgnair23/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/govindgnair23","id":7546100,"login":"govindgnair23","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1NDYxMDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/govindgnair23/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/govindgnair23/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/govindgnair23/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/govindgnair23/starred{/o