them would\nmake the changelog disagree with the tag that shipped. Checked rather than argued:\n\n  git show v0.2.0:CHANGELOG.md   -> 0 mentions of the fan-out in the 0.2.0 section\n  gh release view v0.2.0         -> 0 mentions in the published notes\n\nSo the 0.2.0 section at HEAD was not a historical truth needing preservation. It\nwas fan-out text I appended to that section AFTER the tag was cut, which is\nmisfiled rather than accurate, and the tag''s own notes already disclosed the\nre-tag and stated it was comment-only. Nothing 0.2.0 advertised was wrong.\n\nThe 0.2.0 section is now byte-identical to the one at the v0.2.0 tag, and the\nfan-out is described under the version that actually contains it.\n\nMy published 0.2.1 release notes repeat the claim this corrects. Release bodies\nare editable; tags are not, so the notes get corrected and the tag stays put.\n\nbuild + typecheck + humanize-history suite green.","tree":{"sha":"4890d8d9364dd8d87a8c7ae9f844c4d766a96ef6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/4890d8d9364dd8d87a8c7ae9f844c4d766a96ef6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/3cf3f9b216eaed1b1eeecb7cc068dbe3275f3993","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/3cf3f9b216eaed1b1eeecb7cc068dbe3275f3993","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDNjZjNmOWIyMTZlYWVkMWIxZWVlY2I3Y2MwNjhkYmUzMjc1ZjM5OTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/bf2738c0d113831b379f0b52f9935f663a9d7c1f","sha":"bf2738c0d113831b379f0b52f9935f663a9d7c1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/bf2738c0d113831b379f0b52f9935f663a9d7c1f"}],"sha":"3cf3f9b216eaed1b1eeecb7cc068dbe3275f3993","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/3cf3f9b216eaed1b1eeecb7cc068dbe3275f3993"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/bf2738c0d113831b379f0b52f9935f663a9d7c1f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T01:07:55Z","email":"mayor@localhost","name":"mayor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T01:07:55Z","email":"mayor@localhost","name":"mayor"},"message":"release: 0.2.1 -- ship the fan-out and its cache-source guard forward\n\nv0.2.0 was published and then its tag was moved 18 minutes later to a later commit.\nThat tag therefore advertised the detail fan-out as part of 0.2.0 while the commit it\nnamed did not contain it. This release ships the difference forward instead of moving\na published tag a second time.\n\nThe changelog says so in the release itself rather than leaving the reader to infer\nit: the 0.2.0 section describes work that reached users in 0.2.1, and it is left in\nplace because rewriting it would make the file disagree with the tag that shipped.\n\n0.2.1''s fix is readFromGoofish: a batch answered entirely from search_card_cache was\ncounting as ''the site refused us'', so the rest of the walk went serial for no reason.\n\nbuild + typecheck green; full suite run before tagging.","tree":{"sha":"324a36e6b57d46bf5ac6888492a963b96a99ae70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/324a36e6b57d46bf5ac6888492a963b96a99ae70"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/bf2738c0d113831b379f0b52f9935f663a9d7c1f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/bf2738c0d113831b379f0b52f9935f663a9d7c1f","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKGJmMjczOGMwZDExMzgzMWIzNzlmMGI1MmY5OTM1ZjY2M2E5ZDdjMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/93b1b27c8d3b2ab4ed9e1dd7fd4694c1b15685e0","sha":"93b1b27c8d3b2ab4ed9e1dd7fd4694c1b15685e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/93b1b27c8d3b2ab4ed9e1dd7fd4694c1b15685e0"}],"sha":"bf2738c0d113831b379f0b52f9935f663a9d7c1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/bf2738c0d113831b379f0b52f9935f663a9d7c1f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/93b1b27c8d3b2ab4ed9e1dd7fd4694c1b15685e0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T01:00:11Z","email":"mayor@localhost","name":"mayor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T01:00:11Z","email":"mayor@localhost","name":"mayor"},"message":"fix(xi-byu): land the fan-out guard and its tests, which the previous merge missed\n\nThe previous merge took e06a663, the parent. The branch had moved to e88bba7, a\nchild carrying the last correctness fix and the tests that cover it, so 238 lines\nof tests and the fix they pin never landed. The witness caught this and was right;\nI had verified ancestry for the branch I merged and not the branch''s current tip.\n\nThe fix: a batch that came back empty is only a throttled site if goofish actually\nanswered nothing. readFromGoofish() excludes search_card_cache hits, which are an\nanswer from this process''s own cache rather than from the site. Before it, a batch\nserved entirely from cache counted as ''the site refused us'' and the rest of the call\nwas needlessly walked serially.\n\nConflicts resolved to dag''s side in test/invariants.test.ts and README.md: his\nversion keeps the ordering assertions and adds delegation checks for both navigation\nentry points plus a guard that neither navigates on its own. My README side still\ndescribed detail as ''walked serially'', which is stale the moment the fan-out lands.\n\n141/141 (was 136 - the 5 missing tests are the ones this restores).","tree":{"sha":"a167b809de432dc195f86ffdd7efde006a846d3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/a167b809de432dc195f86ffdd7efde006a846d3a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/93b1b27c8d3b2ab4ed9e1dd7fd4694c1b15685e0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/93b1b27c8d3b2ab4ed9e1dd7fd4694c1b15685e0","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDkzYjFiMjdjOGQzYjJhYjRlZDllMWRkN2ZkNDY5NGMxYjE1Njg1ZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/3942660fb030bb948f72754845479a009ad6a205","sha":"3942660fb030bb948f72754845479a009ad6a205","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/3942660fb030bb948f72754845479a009ad6a205"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/e88bba790b5dd796501d9864cb2daaf2e4627d89","sha":"e88bba790b5dd796501d9864cb2daaf2e4627d89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/e88bba790b5dd796501d9864cb2daaf2e4627d89"}],"sha":"93b1b27c8d3b2ab4ed9e1dd7fd4694c1b15685e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/93b1b27c8d3b2ab4ed9e1dd7fd4694c1b15685e0"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/e88bba790b5dd796501d9864cb2daaf2e4627d89/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T00:49:23Z","email":"refinery@gastown","name":"dag"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T00:49:23Z","email":"refinery@gastown","name":"refinery"},"message":"perf: a bounded parallel detail fan-out for search_items(detail=N) (xi-byu)\n\nsearch_items(detail=N) costs one page load per listing, 13.4s warm median, so\ndetail: 50 is about eleven minutes of one listing after another. Loading four at\nonce was measured on this site and not built, because it needed four DOM pages\nand the fan-out loop is search_items'' own. The loop now has the pages.\n\nMeasured: 66.3s -> 27.1s of wall clock for 4 listings (2.4x, not 4x), and that\nis the honest half -- each listing''s *own* latency went 11.4s -> 20.5s, and on a\nthrottled site four-at-once answered 0/4 where the serial walk still answered\n2/4. Batching turns a per-listing latency problem into an all-or-nothing one.\n\nSo it ships at width 2, not 4 (XIANYU_DETAIL_FANOUT, 0-4, clamped by\nDETAIL_POOL_MAX), each slot on its own page and its own mtop tap, never the\nshared domPage that is holding the results this call is deepening. The pool is\nreachable only from inside the lock search_items already takes. The first batch\nthat comes back with no answer at all turns the fan-out off for the rest of the\ncall and says so in detail_fanout.fell_back. The guard reads what goofish\nanswered, not whether a listing came back: a dead batch falls back to the search\ncard, which is ok for every listing, so a check on ok would have kept the\nfan-out running exactly when it was buying nothing.\n\nNavigation is now one function (Session.loadInto) that open() and\nfanoutSurface() both go through, because a second navigation site is a second\nplace the allowlist check can be left out. Per-load verdicts travel with the\nlease rather than on the session, because two loads in flight at once would\notherwise overwrite each other''s.\n\nEvery listing reports its own ms, via and slot; detail_fanout reports the width,\nthe batches and whether it backed off. XIANYU_DETAIL_FANOUT=0 is the exact\nserial walk that shipped before any of this.","tree":{"sha":"9baa719de6a7ac8e99b1c8986becef26d24a7719","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/9baa719de6a7ac8e99b1c8986becef26d24a7719"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/e88bba790b5dd796501d9864cb2daaf2e4627d89","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/e88bba790b5dd796501d9864cb2daaf2e4627d89","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKGU4OGJiYTc5MGI1ZGQ3OTY1MDFkOTg2NGNiMmRhYWYyZTQ2MjdkODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/e06a6633639264a71d4f8826fdc75244da6729f3","sha":"e06a6633639264a71d4f8826fdc75244da6729f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/e06a6633639264a71d4f8826fdc75244da6729f3"}],"sha":"e88bba790b5dd796501d9864cb2daaf2e4627d89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/e88bba790b5dd796501d9864cb2daaf2e4627d89"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/3942660fb030bb948f72754845479a009ad6a205/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T00:37:26Z","email":"mayor@localhost","name":"mayor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T00:37:26Z","email":"mayor@localhost","name":"mayor"},"message":"perf: fan the detail reads out across a leased pool instead of walking them (xi-byu)\n\nFour DOM pages instead of one, leased in parallel and awaited together, so a batch of\nlisting details costs one page-load latency rather than N. The slot is optional: a\nsession with no pool walks serially under the same envelope, and that fallback is\nreported rather than raised.\n\nThe fan-out refuses to batch when the site has stopped answering. Zero answers in a\nbatch is the throttled-site signal, measured (four pages at once returned 0/4 where\nthe serial walk still answered 2/4), so batching must never be the reason a listing is\nmissed - the rest of the call falls back to the shared page and says so.\n\nTests: ''both navigation sites re-check the URL'' now asserts open() and\nfanoutSurface() both funnel through loadInto, which is where the three allowlist\nchecks live after this refactor, rather than asserting they sit inline in open().\nThe ''rails.join'' assertion accepts either quote style because the built form\nre-quotes string literals; that one was already failing on 305fbec, independently of\nthis work.\n\nBoth mutations were verified to fail the updated test: deleting the post-mtop\nallowlist check, and making open() call page.goto directly.\n\nbuild + typecheck + 136/136 green.","tree":{"sha":"ecfb37ae51a302844cce9b38fbb7e7c7f17be2c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/