42Z","email":"refinery@gastown","name":"refinery"},"message":"merge: probe gating freshness answer ahead of browser launch (xi-cln)","tree":{"sha":"fda49488c38d432d414bfe26e07cb5b72afccff4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/fda49488c38d432d414bfe26e07cb5b72afccff4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/4f43d182b6aae5ebcde0dabcf525927b86005bef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/4f43d182b6aae5ebcde0dabcf525927b86005bef","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDRmNDNkMTgyYjZhYWU1ZWJjZGUwZGFiY2Y1MjU5MjdiODYwMDViZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","sha":"92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/1c8293de64b6da6c7f0719d0735d25c2b2b87223","sha":"1c8293de64b6da6c7f0719d0735d25c2b2b87223","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/1c8293de64b6da6c7f0719d0735d25c2b2b87223"}],"sha":"4f43d182b6aae5ebcde0dabcf525927b86005bef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/4f43d182b6aae5ebcde0dabcf525927b86005bef"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/c1f4b7f51497cb68c91fd5734661a3a2f872e925/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T18:19:40Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"organic"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T18:19:40Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"docs: wrap the probe bound like the constants beside it (xi-r6q)\n\nThe rewrite moved this comment above its trailing position in meaning but left it\ntrailing on the line: 254 columns, where the other constants in the block carry\ntheir note on the three lines above and wrap at ~100. It read as the one\nover-long line in the file rather than as part of the block.\n\nComment only. Verified by transpiling both revisions with removeComments and\ncomparing the emitted tokens: identical.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bd1ba49628a288bdca96e59297c062816747f4d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/bd1ba49628a288bdca96e59297c062816747f4d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/c1f4b7f51497cb68c91fd5734661a3a2f872e925","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/c1f4b7f51497cb68c91fd5734661a3a2f872e925","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKGMxZjRiN2Y1MTQ5N2NiNjhjOTFmZDU3MzQ2NjFhM2EyZjg3MmU5MjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/a140c7cf9ae73c797d9495376db5427938fe6378","sha":"a140c7cf9ae73c797d9495376db5427938fe6378","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/a140c7cf9ae73c797d9495376db5427938fe6378"}],"sha":"c1f4b7f51497cb68c91fd5734661a3a2f872e925","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/c1f4b7f51497cb68c91fd5734661a3a2f872e925"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/b8b3f308fc655eef6bffe3d07f8ef31f6d5d091f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T18:12:49Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"imperator"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T18:15:50Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"chore: name the five commits the harness wrote, and say why the other nineteen stay (xi-ujc)\n\nOf the twenty-four commits on origin/main, four carry the subject `WIP:\ncheckpoint (auto)`, an empty body, the ambient `user <user@localhost>`\nidentity instead of a worker''s, and committer dates inside a four-second\nwindow at 12:43:12-13 on 2026-10-04 while their author dates say 17:08,\n17:15, 17:26 and 06:27. One machine wrote four commits it had made hours\napart. A fifth, 4acf626, is hand-written and merely opens by calling itself\nWIP while shipping src/cache.ts; a sixth (c554385) is the same safety net\nin a different spelling and is not on origin/main at all.\n\ndocs/git-history-humanize.md argues each of the five from the diff and gives\na case for leaving the other nineteen alone, quoting the subject and naming\nwhat it commits to. The general case is that a humanizer over those nineteen\nhas only two options: leave the sentences, or make them less specific.\n\nscripts/humanize-history.mjs makes the retitles. It rebuilds each commit as\na raw object through hash-object rather than commit-tree or filter-branch,\nbecause those two rebuild the header from parsed fields and can tidy a\nmessage or normalize a date -- and the committer timestamps are the only\nproof that the four are a harness artifact. It refuses on subject drift and\non signed commits, and re-reads every object it writes to check the tree,\nboth identity lines, the parents and the message bytes. --apply writes\nrefs/heads/humanized/<tip> and stops: no branch, no tag, no network.\n\nTwo bugs the new tests caught, both of which produced a rewrite that passed\nevery check except the one that mattered. The parent-line parser reset its\nown index when it left the parent block, so a rebuilt commit kept its old\nparent and gained the new one as a second line. writeCommit then rebuilt\nthe message from the parsed commit rather than the retitled one, so the\nrewrite changed every sha and no subject. The assertion that a commit whose\nparents came out unchanged must hash back to itself is what found the first;\nthe one that a sha above the edit must move found the second.\n\nKnown and not fixed: the rewrite orphans refs/tags/v0.1.0, which points at\n9b5b656 -- a descendant of all four checkpoints -- so the published release\nlink breaks and the tag needs re-pointing by hand. xi-e9o carries the\nseparate question of the eleven probe*.mjs scratch scripts at the repo root.","tree":{"sha":"54147c2aea955217e2c0a9634e0abf7d3941c613","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/54147c2aea955217e2c0a9634e0abf7d3941c613"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/b8b3f308fc655eef6bffe3d07f8ef31f6d5d091f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/b8b3f308fc655eef6bffe3d07f8ef31f6d5d091f","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKGI4YjNmMzA4ZmM2NTVlZWY2YmZmZTNkMDdmOGVmMzFmNmQ1ZDA5MWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","sha":"92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30"}],"sha":"b8b3f308fc655eef6bffe3d07f8ef31f6d5d091f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/b8b3f308fc655eef6bffe3d07f8ef31f6d5d091f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/9bd8f525b4765f06a3b4ceb214083e0783be1929/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T18:13:24Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"ace"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T18:13:24Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"docs: three source headers that led with the pitch instead of the rule (xi-j1l)\n\nsrc/index.ts opened with one comment doing three jobs at once: what the file is, a note about\nthe config snippet that used to sit in it, and the account-free pitch.  The pitch is the\n`instructions` string nine lines below and the README lede, so the file comment was its third\ncopy in the same file.  It went, and what is left says how a client runs this and points at the\ntwo places the rest of it lives.\n\nRewriting it surfaced that the old comment was wrong about the config, not just clumsy.  It read\n\"`node /path/to/xianyu-mcp/dist/index.js` as `command` + `args`\"; the README block shows\n`\"command\": \"node\"` with the installed path in `args`.  The comment was the thing that was wrong\nabout a working config block, so the comment is what changed.\n\nsrc/errors.ts had the same shape at twenty lines: the contract fact, five class meanings, the\nGatedError split, the anonymous-search fact, the decline mechanism and the design decision, all\nin one unbroken paragraph, so nothing in it could be skimmed or cited by line.  It is now the\nblock-comment shape build-info.ts already establishes in this repo, with the six classes on\ntheir own lines and the reason for raising instead of returning the 猜你喜欢 rail in its own\nparagraph.\n\nThe 12.4s / 15-41s attribution now names the mayor for the second figure, which is what\nbrowser.ts has said about the same measurement since it was taken.  build.ts''s comment on\n`reasons` gained the nine-commit callback it was already reaching for.\n\nA verbatim claim checked rather than asserted: compiling HEAD''s three files and these three with\nthe same tsc flags and diffing the emitted JavaScript shows the only differences are comment\ntext.  Every declaration, expression and string is byte-identical, the `instructions` string\nincluded -- it is protocol output the client reads, so rewriting it would have been a behavior\nchange and was left alone.\n\nVerified in this worktree: npm run build clean, npm run typecheck clean, node --test 130/130.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"43dce3ec319a5f83d7be88faaa35a019af2bfd95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/43dce3ec319a5f83d7be88faaa35a019af2bfd95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/9bd8f525b4765f06a3b4ceb214083e0783be1929","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/9bd8f525b4765f06a3b4ceb214083e0783be1929","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDliZDhmNTI1YjQ3NjVmMDZhM2I0Y2ViMjE0MDgzZTA3ODNiZTE5Mjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/dfc6d8f8a31751acfdc1fe25648f9122ac634ac1","sha":"dfc6d8f8a31751acfdc1fe25648f9122ac634ac1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/dfc6d8f8a31751acfdc1fe25648f9122ac634ac1"}],"sha":"9bd8f525b4765f06a3b4ceb214083e0783be1929","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/9bd8f525b4765f06a3b4ceb214083e0783be1929"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/dfc6d8f8a31751acfdc1fe25648f9122ac634ac1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T18:12:59Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"ace"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T18:12:59Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"docs: the em dash and the bolded claim, the two tells chy does not have (xi-j1l)\n\nEvery paragraph in these three files opened with a bolded claim, and every em dash in the\nrepository sat in prose while none sat in the maintainer''s own commits.  Neither is how this\nmaintainer writes.  Measured rather than assumed: chy README bold=0 em-dash=0, chy/chy script\nbold=0 with 27 `--`, chy commit bodies em-dash=0 with 24 `--`, and the last fifty commit bodies\nin this repo em-dash=0.  The dash was the outlier -- 88 in README, 32 in CHANGELOG, 2 in\nSECURITY -- and it is now 0 in all three.\n\nBold stops marking claims and starts marking values.  Thirteen paragraph openers and eleven\nguarantee bullets lost the bold that had made every paragraph the same shape.  What is left\nmarks a measured number in a table, a tool name, or an endpoint ret, which is what bold is for.\nNothing that needed finding stopped being findable.\n\nA mechanical pass alone would have left three things wrong, and they are what makes a dash sweep\nworth doing by hand rather than by sed.  README repeated one paragraph verbatim -- \"The server\nruns windowed and needs a display.\" ran after the env-var table and again under Latency -- so the\nsecond copy is gone.  Two table cells used the em dash as an empty placeholder and would have\nread as a divider, so `capabilities` now takes `none` and the cold-start row says why it has no\nresult.  Three dashes were holding a clause together that a colon was the right join for.\n\n`npm test  # __COUNT__ tests` was a placeholder nobody ever stamped.  130 measured in this\nworktree, 130 written down.\n\nCHANGELOG''s two version headings now use the hyphen that the Keep a Changelog format the file\ncites in its own header actually specifies.  Version numbers, dates, entry order and every fact\nare untouched; that file is prose voice only, as the bead asks.\n\nVerified in this worktree: npm run build clean, npm run typecheck clean, node --test 130/130.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b88f7fe5069c4f0371e4ed761c7ead4ba13e4caf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/b88f7fe5069c4f0371e4ed761c7ead4ba13e4caf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/dfc6d8f8a31751acfdc1fe25648f9122ac634ac1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/dfc6d8f8a31751acfdc1fe25648f9122ac634ac1","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKGRmYzZkOGY4YTMxNzUxYWNmZGMxZmUyNTY0OGY5MTIyYWM2MzRhYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","sha":"92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30"}],"sha":"dfc6d8f8a31751acfdc1fe25648f9122ac634ac1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/dfc6d8f8a31751acfdc1fe25648f9122ac634ac1"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/0b2f254df7560b9cca0ca2ae88d786a447d968d8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T18:00:24Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"valkyrie"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T18:00:24Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"extract: comments as sentences, at the width the file already uses\n\nThe two file-header docs were single physical lines, 1100 and 700 characters,\nso a reader who opens the file sees one line per contract and skips it; every\nother block in the tree already wraps near 100 columns and scrolls like prose.\nRewrapped to the width tools.ts and browser.ts already use.\n\nSome blocks opened by restating the mechanism before saying anything a line of\ncode could not. \"This is the whole reason item_view is honest now\", \"This is\nthe only way to get past 30 results\" -- the reason is the point, so it leads.\nThe rest was reflow and rewrap only.\n\nThe measurements and the deliberate absences all stay: 70,146 listings,\n8-14s shell, 6 live listings with an empty title, 58 A / 2 B, the 240s\nevaluate bound, ipLocation deliberately unread, province never parsed out of a\ncity, free_shipping never inferred from an absent fee.\n\nNo line of logic moved. Compiling both revisions with --removeComments and\ndiffing the emitted JS comes out byte-identical, so the change is provably\nprose. Build, typecheck, 130/130 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: space-bunny-free <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f5b1bcdf3431c9b4a258a4662c5cca6caaeadc30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/f5b1bcdf3431c9b4a258a4662c5cca6caaeadc30"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/0b2f254df7560b9cca0ca2ae88d786a447d968d8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/0b2f254df7560b9cca0ca2ae88d786a447d968d8","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDBiMmYyNTRkZjc1NjBiOWNjYTBjYTJhZTg4ZDc4NmE0NDdkOTY4ZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","sha":"92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30"}],"sha":"0b2f254df7560b9cca0ca2ae88d786a447d968d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/0b2f254df7560b9cca0ca2ae88d786a447d968d8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/c13a855e6d630c6a553380431d63f0749633209c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T18:00:06Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"keeper"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T18:00:06Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"docs: the comments in tools.ts stop arguing with themselves (xi-iyv)\n\n511 comment lines and almost none of them were wrong. What they were doing\nwas closing every block with a rhetorical tail -- \"X, rather than Y\", \"X,\nwhich is why Y\", \"so a caller can decide whether to\" -- and that habit, not\nthe vocabulary, is what reads as machine-written. There are 525 semicolons\nchaining two long clauses into one, four blocks that announce themselves\n(\"the exception that proves it\", \"the interesting part is\", \"the honesty\ncontract\", \"bounded, and honest about it\"), and a handful of 400-character\ncomment runs nobody ever rewrapped.\n\nAgainst alperien/chy, which is the ground truth for this maintainer: the\nmechanism opens the comment, the number follows, and the paragraph stops.\nNo bold, no trailing lesson, no comment about the reader.\n\nRewritten, roughly 90 blocks:\n\n- The tail goes. \"This is the whole of due diligence\" is now \"that question\n  is the whole of due diligence\"; \"Bounded, and honest about it: a false\n  settled is not an error, it just means\" is now \"Bounded. A false settled\n  is not an error: it means\".\n- Sentences split where a semicolon was holding two clauses together, and\n  the comment runs that had never been wrapped are wrapped at the width\n  the rest of the file uses.\n- One comment was factually wrong. sellerStanding''s header said \"the four\n  standing numbers\" and SELLER_PROFILE_FIELDS'' header said \"those four\";\n  both return the seven fields in SELLER_ITEM_PAGE_FIELDS. Corrected to\n  seven. The published note string and the seller_profile description\n  still say four -- that is output text, not a comment, so it is filed as\n  xi-e46 rather than edited here.\n\nEvery measurement, error string, symbol, limit and ref survives byte for\nbyte. No line of code changed: git diff shows every added and removed line\nis a comment. build clean, typecheck clean, 130/130 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com> (xi-iyv)","tree":{"sha":"eb3d515550f2785720af46b5462a9d178c6520e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/eb3d515550f2785720af46b5462a9d178c6520e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/c13a855e6d630c6a553380431d63f0749633209c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/c13a855e6d630c6a553380431d63f0749633209c","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKGMxM2E4NTVlNmQ2MzBjNmE1NTMzODA0MzFkNjNmMDc0OTYzMzIwOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","sha":"92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30"}],"sha":"c13a855e6d630c6a553380431d63f0749633209c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/c13a855e6d630c6a553380431d63f0749633209c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/abd6ab0a521e995d8e1bba37165a304156fbd4d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T17:54:19Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"warboy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T17:54:19Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"docs: the honesty guarantees in build-info and cache, said as facts rather than as an essay (xi-oa8)\n\nComment-only. Both files strip down to the same code with every comment removed,\ncompared line for line; `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm run build` stamps\n92e4e9a, `npm test` 130 pass / 0 fail in 141s.\n\nThe old text in both files said the right things in a voice no maintainer writes.\nThe pattern, over and over: a rule, then a sentence about why the rule exists, then\na second sentence about why *that* sentence matters. \"the trap worth naming, because\nit is the reason a naive version of this check reports a clean bill\", \"the part\nworth arguing about\", \"and that is the part this module exists to prevent\". A reader\nis told twice what the module is for and once what the comment is doing. chy''s\ncomments (chy/chy, 413 comment lines) state the rule and its reason in one breath and\nstop: \"A checksum mismatch and a dead network are different faults; name whichever\nhappened, don''t blame the recipe for an outage.\"\n\nFour tells did the damage:\n\n- Self-describing prose. \"Staleness is published, never silent\" as a `##` heading, and\n  three `**bold**` bullet leads inside a cache.ts block comment. Bold labels and\n  markdown headings are a README register; chy uses bare lowercase section markers\n  and no bold anywhere in 413 lines.\n- Rhetorical scaffolding. \"is not a guess\", \"is the whole point of the module\", \"which\n  is exactly the thing this module exists to prevent\" -- claims about the code''s\n  significance where a fact about the code was available. Same shape as the\n  \"not-X-but-Y\" contrast and the one-line closer.\n- Over-long sentences with the reason smuggled in mid-clause. The 8-line paragraph on\n  why `dirty` is not a serveVerdict rule is now four lines that keep every part of the\n  argument: a rebuild of a dirty tree re-stamps itself dirty, so keying freshness on\n  it rebuilds forever; dirt costs the ability to name a clean commit, which is\n  capabilities'' business.\n- Restated conclusions. \"So the build states its own commit\", \"Hence 45s ... and 120s\n  ...\" -- a summary of a paragraph the reader just finished. The cache header lost two\n  of its three.\n\nEvery concrete detail survives: 5s git timeout, 45s/120s, TTL floor 1s and ceiling\n600s, 64 listings and 16 pages, ~100KB a search page, the 28,791/28,804/28,810 match\ncounter and the ~0.07% drift, 4-10s and ~8s and 4-12s and 5-9.5s and 0.4-2.2s, all\nthree env vars, every error string, and both file-level invariants (the no-throw\nguarantee on the capabilities path; only successes are ever stored). The\n`subject`-not-HEAD rule, the `rev-list --left-right --count` orientation and its\nmeasured-not-assumed note, the skew ceiling on `now`, and the empty-sha case all keep\ntheir reasoning.\n\nNo line of logic moved. `src/build-info.ts` and `src/cache.ts` only.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0bdb5020f99d82108ee88860d009f624e5c85853","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/0bdb5020f99d82108ee88860d009f624e5c85853"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/abd6ab0a521e995d8e1bba37165a304156fbd4d0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/abd6ab0a521e995d8e1bba37165a304156fbd4d0","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKGFiZDZhYjBhNTIxZTk5NWQ4ZTFiYmEzNzE2NWEzMDQxNTZmYmQ0ZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","sha":"92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30"}],"sha":"abd6ab0a521e995d8e1bba37165a304156fbd4d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/abd6ab0a521e995d8e1bba37165a304156fbd4d0"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/a140c7cf9ae73c797d9495376db5427938fe6378/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T17:48:08Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"morsov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T17:48:08Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"docs: browser.ts says what each guard stops (xi-r6q)\n\nThe invariants in this file were already measured and written down. What they\nwere not was written like a guardrail: restate the mechanism, mark the comment''s\nown importance, and say it again further down. \"Each is load-bearing\" tells the\nnext reader nothing the code below it does not. Rewritten to the rule and the\nfailure it prevents, with every number kept where it was.\n\n- The MtopTap doc described `want`, `note` and a `seen` set. No such members\n  exist: the class is replies, waiters, onReply, record, take, clear. It also\n  claimed a known-failed reply is dropped, and record() stores everything.\n  Comment fixed, code left alone.\n- Cut the self-referential aside in `open` (\"is worth its own line\"), the\n  self-certifying \"the honest way to read\" in the header, \"and each is\n  load-bearing\" in warmUp, and the filler \"on purpose\" in the header.\n- \"A live page is taken as proof the browser is alive\" appeared three times in\n  three wordings. Stated once, in ensureLaunched; revive and domReady now point\n  at it instead of repeating it.\n- The probe bound read as a bare claim, so it now carries the same reasoning\n  the mtop wait does: an evaluate runs 90s by default, so the probe needs its\n  own bound or the 6s wait is not the one it claims to be.\n- Line-wrapped to ~100 columns and cut three paragraphs down to two sentences\n  each, so a comment reads at the speed of the rule it carries.\n\nNo logic moved: the diff is comment-only, verified by stripping comments from\nboth revisions and comparing. npm run build, npm run typecheck, npm test 130\npass / 0 fail.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ab416cd528aca441aa45b5c77046aefdd33b0e53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/ab416cd528aca441aa45b5c77046aefdd33b0e53"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/a140c7cf9ae73c797d9495376db5427938fe6378","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/a140c7cf9ae73c797d9495376db5427938fe6378","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKGExNDBjN2NmOWFlNzNjNzk3ZDk0OTUzNzZkYjU0Mjc5MzhmZTYzNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","sha":"92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30"}],"sha":"a140c7cf9ae73c797d9495376db5427938fe6378","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/a140c7cf9ae73c797d9495376db5427938fe6378"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/8bd013b2646aca6fdf4b36373532c2d1e300fa38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:20:37Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"cheedo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:20:37Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"chore: the probe scratch scripts leave the tree, and the tree says so (xi-cdt)\n\nEleven probe*.mjs debug scripts were committed to main. Each one drives Chromium against\nthe live site to answer a single question; none is referenced by src, test, scripts,\npackage.json, CI or the README. The numbers they produced are already written down in\nCHANGELOG.md, and the scripts stay in git history for anyone who wants to re-run a\nmeasurement, so nothing is lost by removing the copy on main.\n\nThe three comments that cited them by filename now cite the measurement (n=7 a side,\n12.4s, 0/8 in 32s) instead of a file the reader cannot open, and .gitignore ignores\n/probe*.mjs at the root so the next one stays local.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3dcac6c923b47a2824612080530baf9245c30c87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/3dcac6c923b47a2824612080530baf9245c30c87"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/8bd013b2646aca6fdf4b36373532c2d1e300fa38","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/8bd013b2646aca6fdf4b36373532c2d1e300fa38","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDhiZDAxM2IyNjQ2YWNhNmZkZjRiMzYzNzM1MzJjMmQxZTMwMGZhMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","sha":"92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30"}],"sha":"8bd013b2646aca6fdf4b36373532c2d1e300fa38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/8bd013b2646aca6fdf4b36373532c2d1e300fa38"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/1c8293de64b6da6c7f0719d0735d25c2b2b87223/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T00:25:23Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"capable"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T00:25:23Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"capabilities: the freshness answer no longer waits for a browser launch (xi-cln)\n\nThe build block -- which commit is answering, and is it behind origin/main --\nwas assembled inside the same payload as the live browser/mtop probes, so a\ncaller who wanted only \"is this deploy current?\" paid a measured 60-90s cold\nChromium launch for an answer that is a pure function of the build stamp, the\nbase ref and the checkout. A browser cannot change that answer, and on a wedged\nChromium the wait was unbounded: one caller filed the server as hung when it\nwas answering, slowly.\n\ncapabilities takes `probe`, default true, so no existing caller changes.\nWith probe:false it returns build, cache and the static payload immediately\nand never calls getSession(). Measured on the real Session, same process,\nback to back: 51ms against 33,520ms.\n\nDeliberately not a second tool, and not a two-stage answer inside one call.\nA separate tool is a second code path to staleness, and the two could disagree\nabout whether a deployment is current -- a worse bug than the latency. An MCP\ntool result is one-shot, so \"freshness first, probes after\" has to be two\ninvocations. Both paths call the same buildBlock(), which is the same\nsrc/build-info.ts logic check-deploy.mjs imports: one staleness rule, tested\nonce.\n\nThe fast path cannot imply a probe it did not run. session_state,\nlogin_probe_ret, feed_reachable and browser_launches come back null on the\nunprobed path rather than their false defaults, and a `probes` block names\nthem under not_measured. feed_reachable:false would assert goofish did not\nanswer when nobody asked, and a freshness gate trusting it would report a\nhealthy server as unreachable. null is the \"could not measure\" idiom\nbuild.stale:null already uses, and the two states stay distinct under failure\ntoo: `unknown` means a probe ran and could not tell, null means none ran.\n\nThe 14-entry credential-scan pin in test/invariants.test.ts is untouched. The\none edit there is the published-argument contract at line ~191, capabilities\n{} -> { probe: true }, which is a broken build if left.\n\nGates: typecheck clean, 114/114 tests, build clean.","tree":{"sha":"fa90265a6c1e2f060575ceec211f2cb944aa9720","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/fa90265a6c1e2f060575ceec211f2cb944aa9720"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/1c8293de64b6da6c7f0719d0735d25c2b2b87223","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/1c8293de64b6da6c7f0719d0735d25c2b2b87223","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDFjODI5M2RlNjRiNmRhNmM3ZjA3MTlkMDczNWQyNWMyYjJiODcyMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/29147bddb6e6303ea00f21aacf434d3d343a0e4b","sha":"29147bddb6e6303ea00f21aacf434d3d343a0e4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/29147bddb6e6303ea00f21aacf434d3d343a0e4b"}],"sha":"1c8293de64b6da6c7f0719d0735d25c2b2b87223","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/1c8293de64b6da6c7f0719d0735d25c2b2b87223"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T15:36:09Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"toast"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:40:11Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"feat: the spawn refuses to serve a dist it cannot vouch for (xi-pas)\n\nA `git pull` fast-forwarded the deployment, `git post-merge` does not fire on\na fast-forward, and nothing rebuilt. Every tool answered, every answer was\nplausible, and nothing said so. Thirteen minutes after it was fixed it was\nstale again.\n\n- scripts/serve.mjs is the launcher an MCP client is pointed at instead of\n  `node dist/index.js`. It compares the build''s stamp against the checkout''s\n  HEAD at every spawn and either execs the server or rebuilds and execs the\n  rebuilt one.\n- It refuses to start if the rebuild cannot produce a dist matching the tree.\n  A loud failure costs one session; a silently stale dist costs every session\n  in the drift window and none of them can tell. No flag and no env var skips\n  it.\n- The gate is the spawn and not the pull because this is a per-session stdio\n  process: there is no restart event to hang a rebuild on, so the spawn is the\n  only place that sees both facts at once. `git post-merge` would have missed\n  exactly the fast-forward it was meant to cover.\n- The hot path costs about 40ms and no network, measured. serveVerdict is new\n  in src/build-info.ts beside deployVerdict and asks the narrower half of the\n  question -- is this dist the build of THIS tree -- because that is the half a\n  rebuild can fix. The full comparison stays check-deploy''s, which the launcher\n  runs only when it is about to rebuild.\n- Two loops it declines to enter: an uncommitted tree is not a stale dist (a\n  rebuild of a dirty tree is itself stamped dirty, so the check would fire\n  forever), and a source file dated in the future is not an edit made after\n  the build (same shape, one clock skew away).\n- Everything it prints goes to stderr. stdout is the JSON-RPC channel, and a\n  diagnostic there presents as a client that cannot start.\n\n(xi-pas)","tree":{"sha":"4909cda595ece7e3ece93d79340309ca18c8a16f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/4909cda595ece7e3ece93d79340309ca18c8a16f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDkyZTRlOWFiZDI3ZmIxZDE4YTFhM2ZkMWRiNzlhNWFmOWZjNTNhMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/3c75906248b75097b7c0321809029247e61b6d24","sha":"3c75906248b75097b7c0321809029247e61b6d24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/3c75906248b75097b7c0321809029247e61b6d24"}],"sha":"92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/92e4e9abd27fb1d18a1a3fd1db79a5af9fc53a30"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/3c75906248b75097b7c0321809029247e61b6d24/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T15:37:47Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"dementus"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:07:30Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"perf: the measurements, the corrected numbers, and the probes that took them (xi-x8x)\n\nitem_view cannot be an SPA route change -- 0/8 answered in 32s against 8/8 for a\nfull load -- and the cache-bust is not the cold load it looks like, so both the\ncode and the docs now say so with the numbers next to them. The parallel fan-out\nis measured in both states and filed rather than built: it wins wall clock when\nthe site is healthy and loses every answer when it is not.","tree":{"sha":"97261888fd1293483ea194e2af12e882dc7f2293","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/97261888fd1293483ea194e2af12e882dc7f2293"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/3c75906248b75097b7c0321809029247e61b6d24","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/3c75906248b75097b7c0321809029247e61b6d24","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDNjNzU5MDYyNDhiNzUwOTdiN2MwMzIxODA5MDI5MjQ3ZTYxYjZkMjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/670db481bc1bfbfe077df09de0f5b982cd9d05a2","sha":"670db481bc1bfbfe077df09de0f5b982cd9d05a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/670db481bc1bfbfe077df09de0f5b982cd9d05a2"}],"sha":"3c75906248b75097b7c0321809029247e61b6d24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/3c75906248b75097b7c0321809029247e61b6d24"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/670db481bc1bfbfe077df09de0f5b982cd9d05a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T15:08:40Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"dementus"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:07:29Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"perf: pay the first load at boot, and name a declined load in seconds (xi-x8x)\n\nThe item page cannot be route-changed and the cache-bust is not the cold load it\nlooks like; both were measured and both are written down where the next reader\nwill hit them. What is left is real: the session''s first load moves off the\nuser''s first call, and a load goofish refuses is now recognised from the\nresponse rather than after a 15s mtop wait and a 32s poll.","tree":{"sha":"69d279b517ab0c63b024586e35ace93104591a8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/69d279b517ab0c63b024586e35ace93104591a8e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/670db481bc1bfbfe077df09de0f5b982cd9d05a2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/670db481bc1bfbfe077df09de0f5b982cd9d05a2","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDY3MGRiNDgxYmMxYmZiZmUwNzdkZjA5ZGUwZjViOTgyY2Q5ZDA1YTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/07f1c64bb0e34e1b8dbb9960762dab3cc399e0e4","sha":"07f1c64bb0e34e1b8dbb9960762dab3cc399e0e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/07f1c64bb0e34e1b8dbb9960762dab3cc399e0e4"}],"sha":"670db481bc1bfbfe077df09de0f5b982cd9d05a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/670db481bc1bfbfe077df09de0f5b982cd9d05a2"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/29147bddb6e6303ea00f21aacf434d3d343a0e4b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T16:14:48Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"capable"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T16:14:48Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"WIP(mid-task xi-cln): capabilities freshness answer no longer waits for a browser launch\n\nINCOMPLETE - do not merge. Gates green so far (typecheck clean, 114/114\ntests), but the bead is not finished: docs and bead notes are not written.\n\nThe change so far: capabilities gains a `probe` argument, default true, so\nthe existing contract is unchanged for every current caller. With probe:false\nit returns the freshness answer (build block, cache, the static payload)\nwithout calling getSession() at all, instead of launching Chromium first.\n\nHonesty contract: the four live-probe keys (session_state, login_probe_ret,\nfeed_reachable, browser_launches) come back null on the unprobed path rather\nthan their false defaults, and a `probes` block names them as unmeasured.\n`feed_reachable: false` would assert the feed did not answer when the truth\nis nobody asked, so null is used - the same idiom as build.stale: null.\n\"unknown\" still means a probe ran and could not tell; null means no probe\nran, and the two are kept distinct.\n\nNot yet done: README/CHANGELOG entries, the bead note explaining the\nprobe-flag decision, and a final full gate run.\n\nCommitted while still on the xi-byi branch name: the branch was never\nre-cut when I was re-hooked from xi-byi to xi-cln, and the pr-workflow\nguard blocks branch-creation commands, so the branch still needs renaming\nto polecat/capable/xi-cln before submission.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"47ee34ab6716bbe360fa9dd8690dc082f61d4221","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/47ee34ab6716bbe360fa9dd8690dc082f61d4221"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/29147bddb6e6303ea00f21aacf434d3d343a0e4b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/29147bddb6e6303ea00f21aacf434d3d343a0e4b","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDI5MTQ3YmRkYjZlNjMwM2VhMDBmMjFhYWNmNDM0ZDNkMzQzYTBlNGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/07f1c64bb0e34e1b8dbb9960762dab3cc399e0e4","sha":"07f1c64bb0e34e1b8dbb9960762dab3cc399e0e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/07f1c64bb0e34e1b8dbb9960762dab3cc399e0e4"}],"sha":"29147bddb6e6303ea00f21aacf434d3d343a0e4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/29147bddb6e6303ea00f21aacf434d3d343a0e4b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/07f1c64bb0e34e1b8dbb9960762dab3cc399e0e4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:51:21Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"capable"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:51:21Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"docs+fix: document the TTL cache, and a comment the conflict swallowed (xi-byi)\n\nThe cache shipped with no documentation at all, which for a feature whose\nwhole promise is \"this answer may be old\" is the wrong default: a caller\nreading the README would have met a `cache` block on a tool answer with no\nidea what it meant or how to turn it off.\n\n- README: what is cached (item detail by id, search pages by (query,page)),\n  what deliberately is not and why (the homepage feed is a different slice\n  each call, so caching it changes meaning rather than saving time), the\n  published `cache` block with its real shape, the three env vars, and a\n  guarantee entry: a cached answer is never indistinguishable from a live one.\n- CHANGELOG: the same under 0.2.0 Added, with the reasoning behind 45s/120s\n  rather than a bare number.\n- The test count in the README was stale (71 -> 113).\n- Restored a comment line that the rebase conflict mangled in readListing.","tree":{"sha":"1660a197d455e757c9069d7e7fa5f85db0c98e98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/1660a197d455e757c9069d7e7fa5f85db0c98e98"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/07f1c64bb0e34e1b8dbb9960762dab3cc399e0e4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/07f1c64bb0e34e1b8dbb9960762dab3cc399e0e4","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDA3ZjFjNjRiYjBlMzRlMWI4ZGJiOTk2MDc2MmRhYjNjYzM5OWUwZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/4acf626e8dce8b7bcb39701ea0511388410bf8b4","sha":"4acf626e8dce8b7bcb39701ea0511388410bf8b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/4acf626e8dce8b7bcb39701ea0511388410bf8b4"}],"sha":"07f1c64bb0e34e1b8dbb9960762dab3cc399e0e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/07f1c64bb0e34e1b8dbb9960762dab3cc399e0e4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/4acf626e8dce8b7bcb39701ea0511388410bf8b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:16:52Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"capable"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T14:30:38Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"WIP: TTL cache for item detail and search pages, staleness published (xi-byi)\n\nA repeat view and a re-paged search were paying for a page load each time: an item\npage is 4-10s, a warm re-search 4-12s, a pager page 5-9.5s. Two things are cached --\nthe listing readListing produced for an item id, and the raw search payload for one\n(query, page) -- and nothing else. browse_feed is deliberately not: two identical\nfeed calls return disjoint inventory, so a repeat there is a different answer rather\nthan a stale copy.\n\nThe rule that shaped the code: a cached answer may never be indistinguishable from a\nlive one. Every answer that can come from the cache publishes hit / age_s / stored_at\n/ ttl_s / key and a sentence saying whether goofish was asked -- on item_view, per\npage of a search, per listing in detail_report, and in capabilities before it is\nrelied on. Misses publish the same block with null ages, so the envelope does not\nchange shape with the route.\n\nreadListing is the single seam, so item_view, search_items'' detail argument and\nresolveSeller''s hop are all covered and none can grow a private one. The check runs\nbefore the navigation, which is the whole saving. Only real reads are stored: the\nsearch-card fallback is not, because pinning a five-field card for the TTL would turn\none degraded read into a window of them. A fully-cached search answers with no page\nin the process at all, through the same relevance guard as a live walk.\n\nTTLs: 45s for a listing (a sold listing served at its old price is the harmful\ncase), 120s for a search page (30 listings being compared, and the detail read is\nwhat re-checks liveness). Overridable per process, XIANYU_CACHE=0 turns it off.\nJustified against the measurements already in the repo -- the match counter drifts\n28,791 / 28,804 / 28,810 inside a session -- rather than picked for feel.\n\nWIP: not re-verified end to end. Typecheck passes. Rebase held by the mayor until\nxi-wisp-m1k lands (it also edits src/tools.ts and test/invariants.test.ts).","tree":{"sha":"8bb9bbd3dd92e1d7b7e897a7c037876aa90ec069","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/8bb9bbd3dd92e1d7b7e897a7c037876aa90ec069"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/4acf626e8dce8b7bcb39701ea0511388410bf8b4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/4acf626e8dce8b7bcb39701ea0511388410bf8b4","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDRhY2Y2MjZlOGRjZThiN2JjYjM5NzAxZWEwNTExMzg4NDEwYmY4YjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/d9ce6a6095e432678d091b1dbfde361d3f3da2df","sha":"d9ce6a6095e432678d091b1dbfde361d3f3da2df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/d9ce6a6095e432678d091b1dbfde361d3f3da2df"}],"sha":"4acf626e8dce8b7bcb39701ea0511388410bf8b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/4acf626e8dce8b7bcb39701ea0511388410bf8b4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/d9ce6a6095e432678d091b1dbfde361d3f3da2df/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:51:09Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"rictus"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:51:09Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"chore: gitignore .pi/ alongside .claude/ and .opencode/ -- gt done''s auto-save safety net committed the harness extension into the MR (xi-rre)","tree":{"sha":"597516f4ae0d6d9453d1a51c6ba68280b99d5b8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/597516f4ae0d6d9453d1a51c6ba68280b99d5b8b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/d9ce6a6095e432678d091b1dbfde361d3f3da2df","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/d9ce6a6095e432678d091b1dbfde361d3f3da2df","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKGQ5Y2U2YTYwOTVlNDMyNjc4ZDA5MWIxZGJmZGUzNjFkM2YzZGEyZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/9a3c44bebedb002acc76a0b036f3caad70a36a0b","sha":"9a3c44bebedb002acc76a0b036f3caad70a36a0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/9a3c44bebedb002acc76a0b036f3caad70a36a0b"}],"sha":"d9ce6a6095e432678d091b1dbfde361d3f3da2df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/d9ce6a6095e432678d091b1dbfde