er"},"message":"WIP: checkpoint (auto)","tree":{"sha":"0deacafae24ee95873142e23425d1bc07eb0d092","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/0deacafae24ee95873142e23425d1bc07eb0d092"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/962182644c820353245d31a78657c005a51bb206","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/962182644c820353245d31a78657c005a51bb206","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDk2MjE4MjY0NGM4MjAzNTMyNDVkMzFhNzg2NTdjMDA1YTUxYmIyMDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/265a1cc5ec7dec78dabaeff9995a733747bfa098","sha":"265a1cc5ec7dec78dabaeff9995a733747bfa098","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/265a1cc5ec7dec78dabaeff9995a733747bfa098"}],"sha":"962182644c820353245d31a78657c005a51bb206","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/962182644c820353245d31a78657c005a51bb206"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/265a1cc5ec7dec78dabaeff9995a733747bfa098/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T12:20:13Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"slit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T12:20:13Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"feat: v0.2 search — env-tunable max-items cap and deeper results (xi-xqq)\n\n- Add XIANYU_SEARCH_MAX_ITEMS (30-300, default 300): clamps both limit\n  and pager-walk depth so a huge walk stays inside XIANYU_SEARCH_BUDGET_S\n- Raise search_items default limit 60 -> 120 and bound it to the pager''s\n  full depth of 300 instead of the shared 500\n- New test: the walk stops at the cap, and the rail is still refused","tree":{"sha":"3bb4fb68d5e937bf2e9b2ea4f20030ba1bd2ca85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/3bb4fb68d5e937bf2e9b2ea4f20030ba1bd2ca85"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/265a1cc5ec7dec78dabaeff9995a733747bfa098","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/265a1cc5ec7dec78dabaeff9995a733747bfa098","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDI2NWExY2M1ZWM3ZGVjNzhkYWJhZWZmOTk5NWE3MzM3NDdiZmEwOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/6462d012998173ea163559f4190e99afd7b52c90","sha":"6462d012998173ea163559f4190e99afd7b52c90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/6462d012998173ea163559f4190e99afd7b52c90"}],"sha":"265a1cc5ec7dec78dabaeff9995a733747bfa098","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/265a1cc5ec7dec78dabaeff9995a733747bfa098"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/6462d012998173ea163559f4190e99afd7b52c90/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T09:10:40Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"furiosa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T09:10:40Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"docs: add a CHANGELOG, and say plainly that the history was squashed\n\nThe repository had no CHANGELOG and no git history to build one from: main\nbegins at a single squashed import of the TypeScript port (7ab7d6b, 2026-09-30)\nand the Python original this is a port of lives on another branch entirely\n(python-original, cfe401d). Rather than reconstruct a history that was never\nrecorded here, the file says so in an \"About this file\" section and then\ndocuments 0.1.0 as release notes -- which is what a reader arriving at a\nsquashed repository actually needs, and what `git log` cannot tell them.\n\n0.1.0 is the state at tag v0.1.0 (9b5b656): eight read-only tools, the two-page\nsession, windowed Chromium, lazy Playwright, and the notes that matter for an\ninstall (the tarball ships prebuilt dist/, and npx playwright install chromium is\nstill required because playwright has no install script).\n\nCHANGELOG.md joins `files` so it ships in the tarball, and README links it from\nthe License section.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com> (xi-z1r)","tree":{"sha":"6cee9bde0eb546653ec4e10a5a007e6d743543e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/6cee9bde0eb546653ec4e10a5a007e6d743543e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/6462d012998173ea163559f4190e99afd7b52c90","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/6462d012998173ea163559f4190e99afd7b52c90","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDY0NjJkMDEyOTk4MTczZWExNjM1NTlmNDE5MGU5OWFmZDdiNTJjOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/f460a6ef11b967ca811fc3bcb4c87aea7b7a7c11","sha":"f460a6ef11b967ca811fc3bcb4c87aea7b7a7c11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/f460a6ef11b967ca811fc3bcb4c87aea7b7a7c11"}],"sha":"6462d012998173ea163559f4190e99afd7b52c90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/6462d012998173ea163559f4190e99afd7b52c90"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/f460a6ef11b967ca811fc3bcb4c87aea7b7a7c11/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T09:10:40Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"furiosa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T09:10:40Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"fix: advertise package.json''s version instead of a second copy of it\n\nsrc/index.ts carried `version: ''0.1.0''` as a literal right beside package.json''s\nown \"0.1.0\", and nothing compared the two. `npm version` moved the package and\nthe MCP handshake went on telling every client the previous release existed --\nwhich is the number a client shows its user when they ask what they are talking\nto. Nothing failed, because nothing read both.\n\nThe entry point now reads ../package.json at startup through createRequire, which\nresolves one level up identically from src/ (run straight from a checkout) and\nfrom dist/ (the prebuilt tarball). npm always ships package.json even though\n`files` does not list it. Verified live rather than by inspection: set the\nversion to 9.9.9-probe and the handshake answered 9.9.9-probe, from both\ndist/index.js and src/index.ts.\n\nThe new invariant asserts the read and scans src/ for a semver literal, so the\nsecond copy cannot come back quietly. That is the suite''s 59th test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com> (xi-z1r)","tree":{"sha":"c9debefd67217543e627acb1e75513b2e14e51dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/c9debefd67217543e627acb1e75513b2e14e51dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/f460a6ef11b967ca811fc3bcb4c87aea7b7a7c11","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/f460a6ef11b967ca811fc3bcb4c87aea7b7a7c11","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKGY0NjBhNmVmMTFiOTY3Y2E4MTFmYzNiY2I0Yzg3YWVhN2I3YTdjMTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/16d361afb823b5c7835e91434548ad01541bf26f","sha":"16d361afb823b5c7835e91434548ad01541bf26f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/16d361afb823b5c7835e91434548ad01541bf26f"}],"sha":"f460a6ef11b967ca811fc3bcb4c87aea7b7a7c11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/f460a6ef11b967ca811fc3bcb4c87aea7b7a7c11"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/16d361afb823b5c7835e91434548ad01541bf26f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T09:10:39Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"furiosa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T09:10:39Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"chore: regenerate package-lock.json for playwright as an optional dependency\n\ne893f85 moved playwright from dependencies to optionalDependencies but left the\nlockfile still describing the old shape: playwright and playwright-core are\nrecorded as required, and the root entry is missing the license, bin and\noptionalDependencies keys npm derives from package.json. `npm ci` reads the\nlockfile, so a fresh install resolved a different graph than `npm install` did,\nand `--omit=optional` would not have spared it the download.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com> (xi-z1r)","tree":{"sha":"740734560286fbfd1f9c4f01feb8aa1badb78f07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/740734560286fbfd1f9c4f01feb8aa1badb78f07"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/16d361afb823b5c7835e91434548ad01541bf26f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/16d361afb823b5c7835e91434548ad01541bf26f","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDE2ZDM2MWFmYjgyM2I1Yzc4MzVlOTE0MzQ1NDhhZDAxNTQxYmYyNmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/9b5b656b43f733d6ed83b4a370e61e3151867b20","sha":"9b5b656b43f733d6ed83b4a370e61e3151867b20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/9b5b656b43f733d6ed83b4a370e61e3151867b20"}],"sha":"16d361afb823b5c7835e91434548ad01541bf26f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/16d361afb823b5c7835e91434548ad01541bf26f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/9b5b656b43f733d6ed83b4a370e61e3151867b20/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T16:24:02Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"mayor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T16:24:02Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"docs: describe Playwright as an optional, lazily-loaded dependency\n\nThe install section still listed playwright as a hard dependency, which\nstopped being true in the previous commit.","tree":{"sha":"0f2494b120d2530344928d2c5d884d5269a6529f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/0f2494b120d2530344928d2c5d884d5269a6529f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/9b5b656b43f733d6ed83b4a370e61e3151867b20","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/9b5b656b43f733d6ed83b4a370e61e3151867b20","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDliNWI2NTZiNDNmNzMzZDZlZDgzYjRhMzcwZTYxZTMxNTE4NjdiMjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/e893f8574a3acc1821056d3fc5e494cf4f914fce","sha":"e893f8574a3acc1821056d3fc5e494cf4f914fce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/e893f8574a3acc1821056d3fc5e494cf4f914fce"}],"sha":"9b5b656b43f733d6ed83b4a370e61e3151867b20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/9b5b656b43f733d6ed83b4a370e61e3151867b20"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/e893f8574a3acc1821056d3fc5e494cf4f914fce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T16:23:35Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"mayor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T16:23:35Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"perf: load Playwright lazily instead of at module scope\n\nImporting playwright at the top of browser.ts cost 4.0s on every server\nstart, measured, before a single tool call ran -- and the four mtop-only\ntools never need a Chromium of their own. The dynamic import in launch()\ndrops module load to ~30ms and moves the 19M (of a 73M tree) dependency off\nthe startup path entirely.\n\nplaywright also moves from dependencies to optionalDependencies, so a\nmissing browser is now a launch-time BrowserError carrying the existing\nLAUNCH_HINT rather than a MODULE_NOT_FOUND at startup. The hint text is\nunchanged; the launch path, the windowed-by-default behaviour and\nXIANYU_BROWSER_PATH / XIANYU_HEADLESS handling are untouched.\n\n58/58 tests still pass, and the suite is hermetic enough that this is the\nexpected outcome -- it drives a fake session and imports no Playwright.\nTypecheck, build and CI''s dist .js-specifier guard all clean.","tree":{"sha":"0974312a51fade62c00ac1cd36b81b4d025c5b59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/0974312a51fade62c00ac1cd36b81b4d025c5b59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/e893f8574a3acc1821056d3fc5e494cf4f914fce","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/e893f8574a3acc1821056d3fc5e494cf4f914fce","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKGU4OTNmODU3NGEzYWNjMTgyMTA1NmQzZmM1ZTQ5NGNmNGY5MTRmY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/5d1bc7b612f723e25317770448c96d4822c31fef","sha":"5d1bc7b612f723e25317770448c96d4822c31fef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/5d1bc7b612f723e25317770448c96d4822c31fef"}],"sha":"e893f8574a3acc1821056d3fc5e494cf4f914fce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/e893f8574a3acc1821056d3fc5e494cf4f914fce"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/5d1bc7b612f723e25317770448c96d4822c31fef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T15:54:53Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"mayor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T15:54:53Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"chore: ignore agent tooling dirs\n\nThe Gas Town worktrees drop .beads/, .claude/, CLAUDE.md and .runtime/ into\nevery clone. Without these entries they show as untracked, which trips the\npolecat cleanup predicate and blocks the whole rig from delegating.","tree":{"sha":"3039a3119d4e8ed3751292f603b255706c25b642","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/3039a3119d4e8ed3751292f603b255706c25b642"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/5d1bc7b612f723e25317770448c96d4822c31fef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/5d1bc7b612f723e25317770448c96d4822c31fef","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDVkMWJjN2I2MTJmNzIzZTI1MzE3NzcwNDQ4Yzk2ZDQ4MjJjMzFmZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/7ab7d6b12a2c276926b8a3682eaa2a57314ce177","sha":"7ab7d6b12a2c276926b8a3682eaa2a57314ce177","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/7ab7d6b12a2c276926b8a3682eaa2a57314ce177"}],"sha":"5d1bc7b612f723e25317770448c96d4822c31fef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/5d1bc7b612f723e25317770448c96d4822c31fef"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/7ab7d6b12a2c276926b8a3682eaa2a57314ce177/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:58:05Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"mayor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:58:05Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"docs: CI badge, corrected test count, and the Python lineage\n\nmain no longer contains the Python original, so say where it went and who\nthe extractors derive from rather than leaving a reader to wonder.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"924b766971170027b4462310c6c715c71f13354f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/924b766971170027b4462310c6c715c71f13354f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/7ab7d6b12a2c276926b8a3682eaa2a57314ce177","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/7ab7d6b12a2c276926b8a3682eaa2a57314ce177","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDdhYjdkNmIxMmEyYzI3NjkyNmI4YTM2ODJlYWEyYTU3MzE0Y2UxNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/c1c08aeccc6ecd42043288bd18b59887197f2540","sha":"c1c08aeccc6ecd42043288bd18b59887197f2540","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/c1c08aeccc6ecd42043288bd18b59887197f2540"}],"sha":"7ab7d6b12a2c276926b8a3682eaa2a57314ce177","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/7ab7d6b12a2c276926b8a3682eaa2a57314ce177"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/c1c08aeccc6ecd42043288bd18b59887197f2540/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:53:36Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"mayor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:53:36Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"test: assert detail_ms is consistent, not that it is nonzero\n\nThe first CI run failed on exactly one test, and it was a real flake rather\nthan a regression: `detail_ms` is the sum of the per-listing read times, and\nthis test drives a fake session that answers with no delay, so three reads\ncan legitimately total 0ms. Asserting `> 0` asks the machine to be slow\nenough -- it passed here on incidental scheduler delay and failed on a\nloaded GitHub runner.\n\nThe field''s job is to let a caller price the next call, so what is worth\nasserting is that it is present and that it agrees with the per-listing\nreport, which is the invariant that would actually break if the accounting\nwere wrong. Scanned the rest of the suite for the same shape; this was the\nonly one.\n\n58/58 pass locally, and the green run on CI is the proof.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9981b4ad65c07e5273c2544c43ca92fd9706a26e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/9981b4ad65c07e5273c2544c43ca92fd9706a26e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/c1c08aeccc6ecd42043288bd18b59887197f2540","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/c1c08aeccc6ecd42043288bd18b59887197f2540","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKGMxYzA4YWVjY2M2ZWNkNDIwNDMyODhiZDE4YjU5ODg3MTk3ZjI1NDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/3122e4788757c42f34e1385239111a60c88706ce","sha":"3122e4788757c42f34e1385239111a60c88706ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/3122e4788757c42f34e1385239111a60c88706ce"}],"sha":"c1c08aeccc6ecd42043288bd18b59887197f2540","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/c1c08aeccc6ecd42043288bd18b59887197f2540"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/3122e4788757c42f34e1385239111a60c88706ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:41:46Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"mayor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:41:46Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"ci: run on main, which is the branch this repo publishes on\n\nThe workflow triggered on master, but the repository''s default branch is\nmain. A push to main would have been green by absence: no runs at all, which\nis indistinguishable from a passing suite until something regresses.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"732844431b3fb176724b1ea0a1e776226fead637","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/732844431b3fb176724b1ea0a1e776226fead637"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/3122e4788757c42f34e1385239111a60c88706ce","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/3122e4788757c42f34e1385239111a60c88706ce","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDMxMjJlNDc4ODc1N2M0MmYzNGUxMzg1MjM5MTExYTYwYzg4NzA2Y2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/3cd6a475e00c6eda1d4486692550d9716cca63a6","sha":"3cd6a475e00c6eda1d4486692550d9716cca63a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/3cd6a475e00c6eda1d4486692550d9716cca63a6"}],"sha":"3122e4788757c42f34e1385239111a60c88706ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/3122e4788757c42f34e1385239111a60c88706ce"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/3cd6a475e00c6eda1d4486692550d9716cca63a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:23:52Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"mayor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:23:52Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"fix: the mtop tools were queued behind every search after all\n\nsrc/browser.ts documents that the four mtop-only tools \"do not take this\nlock, so a 70s search no longer blocks a 1.5s feed call\". That was not\ntrue of the shipped server. index.ts wrapped *every* tool in exclusive():\n\n    envelope = { ok: true, data: await exclusive(() => t.run(args)) };\n\nso the two-page session, which exists precisely so the four fast tools can\nrun on their own page while a slow search navigates another, bought nothing:\nbrowse_feed still waited behind search_items for the whole 70s.\n\nThe test that claimed to prove otherwise passed for the wrong reason. It\ncalled t.run directly, bypassing index.ts, and hand-wrapped only the search\nin exclusive() itself -- so it asserted the library rather than the path a\nreal MCP client takes. That is how the regression survived.\n\nThe lock moves to the tools that need it: the three that read and navigate\nthe shared domPage take it themselves, and index.ts stops wrapping. All\nfour mtop tools touch no DOM path (verified: browseFeed, searchCount,\nsearchSuggest and relatedItems reference no domReady/open/scrape), and\ncapabilities only reads, so all five are left free -- it is the tool an agent\ncalls when something else is stuck, and queueing it behind the stuck search\nwould be perverse.\n\nThe test now drives the registered tool table, the way index.ts does, plus a\nsource-level invariant that fails if exclusive() ever reappears in the entry\npoint and silently re-serialises the fast four again.\n\nAlso in this commit:\n- LICENSE credited `Copyright 2026 fancy`, the upstream Python author of\n  goofish-cli, for a TypeScript port they did not write. It contradicted\n  NOTICE and package.json. Attribution to them belongs in NOTICE, where it\n  already correctly lives.\n- Tool descriptions: every agent session pays for all eight, used or not.\n  search_items alone was 587 of 1,179 tokens -- a changelog of measured\n  latency sitting in a string that loads on every connection. Trimmed to 920\n  total; the measurements moved behind capabilities, which is the tool that\n  already exists to be fetched on demand by an agent about to pay the cost.\n- README opened with \"There is no build step and no dist/\", which is false:\n  main and bin both point at dist/index.js.\n- Dead condition: `!payload.reused` where payload is {} two lines above.\n\n58/58 tests pass, typecheck clean, build emits .js specifiers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"16631a9c8367c0a2a0f054e568fce726a620f608","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/16631a9c8367c0a2a0f054e568fce726a620f608"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/3cd6a475e00c6eda1d4486692550d9716cca63a6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/3cd6a475e00c6eda1d4486692550d9716cca63a6","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDNjZDZhNDc1ZTAwYzZlZGExZDQ0ODY2OTI1NTBkOTcxNmNjYTYzYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/cfa5da15ff07df70dc09d426ed756ca3c2390ed7","sha":"cfa5da15ff07df70dc09d426ed756ca3c2390ed7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/cfa5da15ff07df70dc09d426ed756ca3c2390ed7"}],"sha":"3cd6a475e00c6eda1d4486692550d9716cca63a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/3cd6a475e00c6eda1d4486692550d9716cca63a6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/cfa5da15ff07df70dc09d426ed756ca3c2390ed7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:23:30Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"mayor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T16:23:30Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"feat: item_view reads the page''s own detail reply, and search tops up\n\nWork that was sitting uncommitted, in two stashes and the working tree.\nFour changes, all measured against the live site.\n\nitem_view: the detail call is not ours to make. Re-issuing it through the\npage''s own mtop client with the payload the page sent answers TIMEOUT,\nbecause goofish stamps requests its own bundle originates with a per-call\nanti-bot blob. Letting the page make the call and reading the reply off the\nwire is both the only route that works and the richer one: title, full\ngallery, description and seller statistics, none of which the DOM exposed.\nThis replaces a premise the tool was built on -- that goofish does not serve\nitem pages logged out -- which was documented in three comments and the tool\ndescription, and was wrong.\n\nsearch_items tops up: the pager walk is not deterministic, and a degraded\npage can match far fewer than its 30. Measured across three sessions,\n`pages: 2` yielded 25, 28 and 55 matches of 60 scanned, so a caller asking\nfor 50 listings could be silently short. Up to two more pages are walked\nwhen the pool comes up short of limit, bounded so a thin market cannot turn\na cheap call into an expensive one.\n\nAlso: the mtop readiness probe reports a timeout as \"not ready\" rather than\nraising, so a page still booting is a reason to keep waiting instead of a\nreason to fail the call.\n\n56/56 tests pass, typecheck clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b07f6291b5882404ba60e54e8fbdbe4b812383b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/b07f6291b5882404ba60e54e8fbdbe4b812383b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/cfa5da15ff07df70dc09d426ed756ca3c2390ed7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/cfa5da15ff07df70dc09d426ed756ca3c2390ed7","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKGNmYTVkYTE1ZmYwN2RmNzBkYzA5ZDQyNmVkNzU2Y2EzYzIzOTBlZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/12c7d15628e97a4df6191359bd5e95f8956f2629","sha":"12c7d15628e97a4df6191359bd5e95f8956f2629","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/12c7d15628e97a4df6191359bd5e95f8956f2629"}],"sha":"cfa5da15ff07df70dc09d426ed756ca3c2390ed7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/cfa5da15ff07df70dc09d426ed756ca3c2390ed7"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/12c7d15628e97a4df6191359bd5e95f8956f2629/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T17:40:46Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T17:40:46Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"perf: make the common paths fast without losing the richer answer\n\nAsked whether this was reliable, so measured it instead of asserting it. Two\nruns of 21 calls -- repeated identical queries included, which is what exposes\nflakiness that averages hide -- came back 21/21 both times. Zero failures. But\nmeasuring turned up four real problems, none of which a green suite would have\ncaught.\n\nA wrong or dead id cost 146s. The item page is login-gated most of the time, so\nthe 12-query sweep was doing a dozen page loads to discover an id that does not\nexist. The sweep is now 8 queries inside a 45s ceiling, and a dead id costs ~40s.\n\nThe search-then-view sequence -- the ordinary way anyone uses this -- cost 43s,\nbecause item_view loaded a page that usually answers with the rail. Search\nresults are now remembered per process and the sweep checks that first.\n\nSIGTERM tore the browser down only incidentally. transport.onclose covers a\nclean client disconnect and nothing else, so a supervisor sending SIGINT then\nSIGTERM within a second, or a crash, left the signal path unhandled. Added\nhandlers for all three, re-entrant, plus an exit hook. Verified: SIGTERM now\nexits 0 and leaves no Chromium behind.\n\nAnd one regression I introduced while fixing those: the cache short-circuit\nreturned the 2-field search card even when the page would have supplied ten.\nMeasured before noticing -- missing=8 on every result, where the page route had\nbeen returning missing=0 or 1. The cache now short-circuits only the expensive\nsweep, never the page, so the richer answer wins whenever goofish serves it and\nthe fallback still covers when it does not.\n\n40/40 tests, typecheck clean, and the input-validation sweep still rejects\nevery malformed argument in 0.0s without touching the network.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"866c1a9a223242d9ee5d628f33dd740183926ab1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/866c1a9a223242d9ee5d628f33dd740183926ab1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/12c7d15628e97a4df6191359bd5e95f8956f2629","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/12c7d15628e97a4df6191359bd5e95f8956f2629","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDEyYzdkMTU2MjhlOTdhNGRmNjE5MTM1OWJkNWU5NWY4OTU2ZjI2Mjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/61bacea805f9025dd3ae8f9d5d930db97348fc2c","sha":"61bacea805f9025dd3ae8f9d5d930db97348fc2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/61bacea805f9025dd3ae8f9d5d930db97348fc2c"}],"sha":"12c7d15628e97a4df6191359bd5e95f8956f2629","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/12c7d15628e97a4df6191359bd5e95f8956f2629"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/61bacea805f9025dd3ae8f9d5d930db97348fc2c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T20:45:29Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T20:45:29Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"docs: stop telling readers item_view is broken, and why\n\nThe README still carried the throttling story -- the one I asserted without\nproving and that the data already contradicted. Replaced with what was\nactually measured: the item page is login-gated, the page route works when\ngoofish serves the detail block, and the search route covers when it does not.\n\nThe tool description got the same treatment, since that is what an agent\nactually reads: it now names both sources, says which fields each one can\nreally supply, and says the fallback is keyed on item_id so it cannot return\na similarly-named listing.\n\nLatency table: the two DOM tools are marked ok with the measured numbers, and\nthe table is labelled as the record of what it measured at the time rather\nthan presented as current.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"711a4a05ef63e0fb809df4230ffdeee8dd8d67a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/711a4a05ef63e0fb809df4230ffdeee8dd8d67a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/61bacea805f9025dd3ae8f9d5d930db97348fc2c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/61bacea805f9025dd3ae8f9d5d930db97348fc2c","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDYxYmFjZWE4MDVmOTAyNWRkM2FlOGY5ZDVkOTMwZGI5NzM0OGZjMmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/7cbd7f7eb03352462d44d604814f70b5330d795f","sha":"7cbd7f7eb03352462d44d604814f70b5330d795f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/7cbd7f7eb03352462d44d604814f70b5330d795f"}],"sha":"61bacea805f9025dd3ae8f9d5d930db97348fc2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/61bacea805f9025dd3ae8f9d5d930db97348fc2c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/7cbd7f7eb03352462d44d604814f70b5330d795f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T20:39:22Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T20:39:22Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"fix: item_view works again, and says why when it cannot\n\nI was wrong to call the earlier failures throttling. They were code, and the\nevidence I had already contradicted me: search_count returned 0 for a query\nthat had answered 28,844 twenty minutes earlier, and I noted that and carried\non with the throttling story anyway.\n\nitem_view was not returning listings because of three defects:\n\n1. The readiness poll was clipped to whatever was left of the call''s budget, so\n   a slow load -- 42s to domcontentloaded, 52s to paint, measured -- left the\n   wait almost nothing, and it was watching a page that was merely slow.\n2. waitForMtop''s probe could throw, taking the whole tool call down with it on\n   a page that was still booting. A probe that times out is not a verdict.\n3. Neither the item scraper nor item_view could tell a page that was *answered*\n   from one that was *not yet*: goofish''s own 网络不见了 notice, and a page\n   holding only 猜你喜欢 cards, were both polled for 32s a time, five times\n   over, on content that was never going to change.\n\nThe finding that matters, measured three ways: anonymous item pages are\nlogin-gated. The page''s own item-detail call answers TIMEOUT::接口超时 through\nthe page''s client on both the web and h5 hosts; called directly it answers\nRGV587_ERROR and hands back a passport redirect; and tracked over 120s the\nrendered page never grows 立即购买 or 担保交易, with 为你推荐 at character 18 and\nthe rail below it. The SPA mounts, is refused, and draws the rail.\n\nSo the fix is a second anonymous route rather than more patience. search_items\nreturns real listings with title, price, condition, brand and city, so item_view\nfalls back to it, keyed on item_id rather than the query, and reports\nsource: search_card. The description, the gallery and the seller''s statistics\nexist only behind the login-gated API and are reported in fields_missing rather\nthan invented. Search results are remembered per process, so searching and then\nviewing a result -- the ordinary sequence -- costs a lookup rather than a dozen\npage loads.\n\nMeasured, 6 live listings, search then view: 6/6 in 4-13s. The page route works\nwhen goofish serves the detail block, and the fallback covers when it does not.\nA failure that reaches neither now names the login gate rather than telling the\nreader to look for a throttled IP.\n\n40/40 tests. The closed-mtop-API invariant caught the API name appearing in a\ncomment; the exemption is for naming, not calling, so the name moved rather than\nthe check weakening.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0b5624cc7440f4ef411b98e7fcb7f42f543fcbab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/0b5624cc7440f4ef411b98e7fcb7f42f543fcbab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/7cbd7f7eb03352462d44d604814f70b5330d795f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/7cbd7f7eb03352462d44d604814f70b5330d795f","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDdjYmQ3ZjdlYjAzMzUyNDYyZDQ0ZDYwNDgxNGY3MGI1MzMwZDc5NWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/9a761ad5840b8877d47e11b47c087218046cef5a","sha":"9a761ad5840b8877d47e11b47c087218046cef5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/9a761ad5840b8877d47e11b47c087218046cef5a"}],"sha":"7cbd7f7eb03352462d44d604814f70b5330d795f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/7cbd7f7eb03352462d44d604814f70b5330d795f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/9a761ad5840b8877d47e11b47c087218046cef5a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T15:39:33Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T15:39:33Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"fix: stop the item_view readiness poll from starving its own retries\n\nRaising the poll to 32s in the previous commit fixed the symptom and broke\nthe mechanism: the poll ran to its own limit on the first load, spent the\ncall''s 90s budget there, and the loop exited after 4 attempts having never\ntried the reload that actually rescues a shell. 32s plus the reload settle,\nfive times, needs ~175s, so only the first page was ever waited on.\n\nThe poll is now bounded by the call''s remaining budget as well as its own\nconstant, so it cannot consume the clock the retries need. Measured after\nthe change: the same input that previously used 4 attempts now uses all 5.\n\nitem_view is still not returning listings on this machine. That is the site,\nnot this: a direct Playwright probe holds the item page at the 512-character\nshell for 46s+ where it painted at 26s earlier, browse_feed went from 7.9s\nto 69s, and search_count briefly returned 0 for a query that had answered\n28,844 twenty minutes earlier. The IP is being throttled. The tool reports\nthat honestly -- it raises DetailUnavailableError naming the page text\nrather than returning the shell''s contents as if they were a listing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f8c8c0cf182b3fdf67172309053173c6994d2d92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/f8c8c0cf182b3fdf67172309053173c6994d2d92"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/9a761ad5840b8877d47e11b47c087218046cef5a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/9a761ad5840b8877d47e11b47c087218046cef5a","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDlhNzYxYWQ1ODQwYjg4NzdkNDdlMTFiNDdjMDg3MjE4MDQ2Y2VmNWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/7997317b2b7f738867bff1a6ac23aef211e4c023","sha":"7997317b2b7f738867bff1a6ac23aef211e4c023","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/7997317b2b7f738867bff1a6ac23aef211e4c023"}],"sha":"9a761ad5840b8877d47e11b47c087218046cef5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/9a761ad5840b8877d47e11b47c087218046cef5a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/7997317b2b7f738867bff1a6ac23aef211e4c023/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T15:07:55Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T15:07:55Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"release: publishable packaging, licence, and a README that matches the code\n\nThree of these make the package installable at all; the rest make it honest.\n\nNode refuses to strip TypeScript types from files under node_modules/, so the\ntarball shipped src/*.ts installed cleanly and then died on first run with\nERR_UNSUPPORTED_NODE_MODELS_TYPE_STRIPPING. The published artifact is now\nprebuilt dist/*.js (tsconfig.build.json, which differs from the source config\nonly in emitting). Verified end to end: npm pack -> npm install into a clean\nproject -> stdio initialize, tools/list, and live search_count (28,844 for\nx220) and browse_feed calls, all from node_modules.\n\nprivate:true would have made this unpublishable (EPRIVATE), and there was no\nLICENSE or license field, so npm would have shipped it UNLICENSED. Both fixed.\nThe Apache-2.0 LICENSE and the NOTICE carrying the goofish-cli attribution are\ntaken from the Python implementation of the same server, which this is a port\nof; the NOTICE now says so explicitly rather than leaving the chain implicit.\n\nREADME corrections, each checked against the code rather than remembered:\n\n- XIANYU_SEARCH_BUDGET_S and XIANYU_ITEM_VIEW_BUDGET_S were documented as 45\n  and the code defaults are 150 and 90.\n- The measured-results table reported search_items and item_view as failing.\n  search_items no longer does -- 8/8 live queries, 7 on the first attempt --\n  so the table now says which parts of it are stale instead of implying the\n  tool is broken.\n- Added a section on the searchbox mechanism, which was undocumented: the 2x2x2\n  matrix, why a direct-URL search returns the rail, why the input is focused\n  rather than clicked, and why typing is read back rather than assumed.\n- Install section now states the Node floor and the display requirement, both\n  of which a headless user hits immediately.\n\nThe test suite and the product were left as they were: 40/40, tsc clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4852a33aac3418a89a43de9eb8471d8faaf5779f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/4852a33aac3418a89a43de9eb8471d8faaf5779f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/7997317b2b7f738867bff1a6ac23aef211e4c023","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/7997317b2b7f738867bff1a6ac23aef211e4c023","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDc5OTczMTdiMmI3ZjczODg2N2JmZjFhNmFjMjNhZWYyMTFlNGMwMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/33e5434a2acc167291d6c672c3b2b34ea3cfb627","sha":"33e5434a2acc167291d6c672c3b2b34ea3cfb627","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/33e5434a2acc167291d6c672c3b2b34ea3cfb627"}],"sha":"7997317b2b7f738867bff1a6ac23aef211e4c023","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/7997317b2b7f738867bff1a6ac23aef211e4c023"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/33e5434a2acc167291d6c672c3b2b34ea3cfb627/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:16:23Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:16:23Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"test: teach the harness the searchbox flow; 40/40 green\n\nThe suite was 33/15 against a product that works. The failures were a stale\nharness, not broken code: search_items was rewritten from direct-URL\nnavigation to typing into the SPA''s search box, and makeSession still knew\nonly the three old scrapers, so both new in-page calls answered null.\n\nmakeSession now models the searchbox -- a mounted input, a keyboard, and a\nnavigation on Enter -- and domSession carries a real <input> plus the\nwindow and location globals the in-page scripts read. Both run the actual\nsearch code rather than mocking past it, so the tests exercise the path\nthat ships.\n\nTwo real bugs surfaced while doing this, and both were the product''s:\n\n- The refusal counted log ENTRIES, not attempts. A searchbox attempt logs\n  twice (the typing step, then the scrape), so a 1-attempt call reported\n  \"2 attempt(s)\" and a 3-attempt call reported \"6\" -- telling an operator\n  to raise a budget that was fine. Now counted as distinct attempt numbers.\n\n- item_view''s readiness poll was 6s against a page that takes up to 26s to\n  paint, so it gave up mid-wait and reported a partial success with\n  fields_missing. Raised to 32s, and the call budget to 90s so it is no\n  longer smaller than the work it bounds.\n\nThree assertions were updated because the rewrite legitimately changed what\nthey pinned: the refusal wording, and two that indexed attempt_log[0] --\nnow the typing step, not the scrape. One invariant stopped asserting a\nliteral 700ms delay and asserts the order and rationale instead; its\n\"say why the dialog is left alone\" check caught a doc comment that had\nquietly lost the A/B measurement behind it, now restored.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2db77c3d53ca862d5f9989d15394e9b4319a8279","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/2db77c3d53ca862d5f9989d15394e9b4319a8279"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/33e5434a2acc167291d6c672c3b2b34ea3cfb627","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/33e5434a2acc167291d6c672c3b2b34ea3cfb627","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDMzZTU0MzRhMmFjYzE2NzI5MWQ2YzY3MmMzYjJiMzRlYTNjZmI2Mjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/031a0294a9bae30512b95ce843acfef367552f6d","sha":"031a0294a9bae30512b95ce843acfef367552f6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/031a0294a9bae30512b95ce843acfef367552f6d"}],"sha":"33e5434a2acc167291d6c672c3b2b34ea3cfb627","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/33e5434a2acc167291d6c672c3b2b34ea3cfb627"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/031a0294a9bae30512b95ce843acfef367552f6d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:33:53Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:33:53Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"fix: make search keystrokes verifiable and item_view wait long enough\n\nTwo measured defects, both found by running the tools live.\n\nSEARCH_MARK crossed the Playwright boundary as a closed-over constant, so\nevery search attempt died with \"ReferenceError: SEARCH_MARK is not defined\"\nand 0/4 searches returned anything. The marker is now passed as the in-page\nfunctions'' single argument, the way RAIL_MARKERS already was.\n\ngoofish''s SPA re-renders the search input under the cursor, and a\nkeyboard.type burst spanning a re-render is silently truncated: measured,\n\"thinkpad x220\" landing as \"th\", which then submitted a near-empty keyword\nand served the rail. typeSearch now reads the input back and re-sends\nwhatever did not land, reporting incomplete-keystrokes rather than a\nmisleading refusal.\n\nitem_view polled 6s for a detail block that takes up to 26s to paint on a\nslow link, so it gave up mid-wait and reported a partial success with\nfields_missing: title|want_count. Raised to 32s, and the call budget to 90s\nso it is no longer smaller than the work it bounds.\n\nVerified live against goofish: 8/8 searches, 7 of 8 on the first attempt.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c8f63efecab92bb60f0a07df1c330d0990d2bbba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/c8f63efecab92bb60f0a07df1c330d0990d2bbba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/031a0294a9bae30512b95ce843acfef367552f6d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/031a0294a9bae30512b95ce843acfef367552f6d","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDAzMWEwMjk0YTliYWUzMDUxMmI5NWNlODQzYWNmZWYzNjc1NTJmNmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/9e208d605e248d81bddf89bb3838c83cf6a8abee","sha":"9e208d605e248d81bddf89bb3838c83cf6a8abee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/9e208d605e248d81bddf89bb3838c83cf6a8abee"}],"sha":"031a0294a9bae30512b95ce843acfef367552f6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/031a0294a9bae30512b95ce843acfef367552f6d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/9e208d605e248d81bddf89bb3838c83cf6a8abee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T11:47:21Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T11:47:21Z","email":"user@localhost","name":"user"},"message":"wip: TS port at opencode cancellation point, searchbox fix applied\n\nSnapshot taken before release hardening. search_items is rewritten to the\nsearchbox flow but the test harness still mocks the old one, so 7 tests\nfail for stale-harness reasons rather than product reasons.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5a3975d987dcde1bc832ef37dcdccb007a57f9a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/trees/5a3975d987dcde1bc832ef37dcdccb007a57f9a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/git/commits/9e208d605e248d81bddf89bb3838c83cf6a8abee","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commit/9e208d605e248d81bddf89bb3838c83cf6a8abee","node_id":"C_kwDOUtZTD9oAKDllMjA4ZDYwNWUyNDhkODFiZGRmODliYjM4MzhjODNjZjZhOGFiZWU","parents":[],"sha":"9e208d605e248d81bddf89bb3838c83cf6a8abee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits/9e208d605e248d81bddf89bb3838c83cf6a8abee"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/alperien/xianyu-mcp/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=3cf3f9b216eaed1b1eeecb7cc068dbe3275f3993&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T16%3A02%3A36.093Z"}');
