99/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T01:24:17Z","email":"abhisheknahire89@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Nahire"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T01:24:17Z","email":"abhisheknahire89@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Nahire"},"message":"Add npm run deliver: one-command delivery through the protected gate\n\nscripts/deliver-pr.js encodes the session''s proven delivery flow:\npreflight (fetch, local-main check, protection-rule read), push\nmain:refs/heads/feature/deliver-<sha>, open the PR, poll the `test`\ncheck-run, merge with a merge commit (never squash), publish the\ntruthful \"CI / test\" legacy status via /statuses/<sha> if the gate\nstill answers 405, verify merged state, delete the remote branch, and\nfast-forward local main without touching a dirty worktree.\n\nResume modes for every mid-flow failure: --pr N re-drives an existing\nPR, --branch NAME reuses a pushed branch, --dry-run prints the plan.\nCredentials come from GH_TOKEN or the macOS keychain github.com\ncredential (probed via git credential-osxkeychain; never printed).\n\nBattle-tested on its first real run (PR #6): CI-green merge succeeded\nwith no manual shim; the run caught one real bug — PR.state reads\n\"closed\" for merged PRs, so merged-ness must be checked via the\n`merged` boolean — fixed here.\n\n🤖 Generated with Codebuff\nCo-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>","tree":{"sha":"d6c7891aad906359f6f3fcd365e2ada086c54faa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhisheknahire89/Cancer-HIS-CCA/git/trees/d6c7891aad906359f6f3fcd365e2ada086c54faa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhisheknahire89/Cancer-HIS-CCA/git/commits/7cab1a5132a45d559cffbe6ff04f16ce5b80c599","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/179821703?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhisheknahire89/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com