,{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/179821703?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhisheknahire89/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhisheknahire89/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhisheknahire89/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhisheknahire89/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/abhisheknahire89","id":179821703,"login":"abhisheknahire89","node_id":"U_kgDOCrfchw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhisheknahire89/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhisheknahire89/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhisheknahire89/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhisheknahire89/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhisheknahire89/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhisheknahire89","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhisheknahire89/Cancer-HIS-CCA/commits/358f5838afc833abbb46b53778c7808a56abc62a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:15:42Z","email":"abhisheknahire89@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Nahire"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:15:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"CCA OS oncology platform with automatic disease-specific staging engine (#1)\n\nCCA OS oncology platform with automatic disease-specific staging engine\n\nInitial commit of the cca-os implementation: OpenMRS-aligned REST backend,\nbrowser UI, and the staging/classification pipeline the CCA clinical mandate\nrequires — declarative content packs (never engine if/else, never eval),\nserver-authoritative derivation, clinician sign-gate, derivation trace.\n\nFour features delivered in this thread, all proven through the real surface:\n\n- Staging content-pack loader: validated versioned pack files (supersedes\n  discipline, fail-closed skip-and-report, admin registry + governed reload),\n  with a PoC breast cTNM pack driving automatic derivation in the browser.\n- §31 flag-discrepancy flow: Flag discrepancy on signed staging results routes\n  a review task; the task opens the form pre-filled from the flagged facts,\n  the engine re-derives, and the superseding signature resolves the flag.\n- Staging-window evidence auto-suggestion (§24/§25): focused staging facts\n  surface candidate labs/imaging/pathology from the relevant staging window\n  for one-click confirmation; one shared owner builds the evidence-item shape\n  for both the suggestion strip and the evidence picker.\n- Licensed-AJCC adapter PoC: env credentials + ACTIVE licence record gate a\n  fetch → validate → register loop into the engine pack seam; proven over real\n  HTTP against a stub server (credential flow asserted, fail-closed branches\n  keep the registry untouched), derivation and sign gate byte-identical.\n\nDeterministic engine statuses (NEEDS_INFORMATION / AMBIGUOUS /\nCONTENT_PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE / INVALID_INPUT) prevent any guessed stage;\nnon-TNM disease (myeloma ISS/R-ISS) runs the same pipeline without T/N/M.\n\nVerification at commit time: npm test exit 0 — 11 unit suites (363 checks\nincl. adapter 31 + wire 20 + suggestions 17 + flag 13) and two Playwright\nreal-Chrome demo harnesses (breast 36/36, myeloma 34/34); live server booted\non this tree (HTTP 200) with the admin content-pack registry rendering clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with Codebuff\nCo-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>","tree":{"sha":"1283fce4c16e315203600c0e5ebe5d761d72d8e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhisheknahire89/Cancer-HIS-CCA/git/trees/1283fce4c16e315203600c0e5ebe5d761d72d8e9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abhisheknahire89/Cancer-HIS-CCA/git/commits/358f5838afc833abbb46b53778c7808a56abc62a","verification":{"payload":"tree 1283fce4c16e315203600c0e5ebe5d761d72d8e9\nparent a44df971bf14718bebbae38b3074953e16ee3dad\nauthor Abhishek Nahire <abhisheknahire89@gmail.com> 1790518542 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790518542 +0530\n\nCCA OS oncology platform with automatic disease-specific staging engine (#1)\n\nCCA OS oncology platform with automatic disease-specific staging engine\n\nInitial commit of the cca-os implementation: OpenMRS-aligned REST backend,\nbrowser UI, and the staging/classification pipeline the CCA clinical mandate\nrequires — declarative content packs (never engine if/else, never eval),\nserver-authoritative derivation, clinician sign-gate, derivation trace.\n\nFour features delivered in this thread, all proven through the real surface:\n\n- Staging content-pack loader: validated versioned pack files (supersedes\n  discipline, fail-closed skip-and-report, admin registry + governed reload),\n  with a PoC breast cTNM pack driving automatic derivation in the browser.\n- §31 flag-discrepancy flow: Flag discrepancy on signed staging results routes\n  a review task; the task opens the form pre-filled from the flagged facts,\n  the engine re-derives, and the superseding signature resolves the flag.\n- Staging-window evidence auto-suggestion (§24/§25): focused staging facts\n  surface candidate labs/imaging/pathology from the relevant staging window\n  for one-click confirmation; one shared owner builds the evidence-item shape\n  for both the suggestion strip and the evidence picker.\n- Licensed-AJCC adapter PoC: env credentials + ACTIVE licence record gate a\n  fetch → validate → register loop into the engine pack seam; proven over real\n  HTTP against a stub server (credential flow asserted, fail-closed branches\n  keep the registry untouched), derivation and sign gate byte-identical.\n\nDeterministic engine statuses (NEEDS_INFORMATION / AMBIGUOUS /\nCONTENT_PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE / INVALID_INPUT) prevent any guessed stage;\nnon-TNM disease (myeloma ISS/R-ISS) runs the same pipeline without T/N/M.\n\nVerification at commit time: n