,"gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anujgawde","id":87605577,"login":"anujgawde","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NjA1NTc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anujgawde/gridline/commits/d2a2a8db01e6eefbee782df48683f7b834af1eb5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T02:29:15Z","email":"gawdeanuj@gmail.com","name":"anujgawde"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T02:29:15Z","email":"gawdeanuj@gmail.com","name":"anujgawde"},"message":"fix(viewer): bound the pinned tile set with its own budget\n\nLevels 0 and 1 were exempt from the cache budget so a revisited sheet\ncould repaint from memory. The exemption had no ceiling, and at fit\nscale every tile the renderer needs is a coarse one, so eviction never\nran: 700 MB of pixels over 140 sheets, growing 5 MB a sheet without\nbound. The reasoning behind the exemption used the encoded size of a\ntile, ~13 KB, against the 1 MB it occupies decoded.\n\nThe pinned tier now has a budget of its own, evicted by least-recently-\nused sheet rather than by tile, since four of a sheet''s five coarse\ntiles paints a sheet with a hole in it. Expressed in bytes rather than\nsheets because coarse cost is page geometry: five tiles for any\nstandard landscape size, eight for portrait.\n\nPixels now plateau at 160 MB from sheet 33 through 140.","tree":{"sha":"f1c30301c31b98b35fca8a87a141937de16a13ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anujgawde/gridline/git/trees/f1c30301c31b98b35fca8a87a141937de16a13ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anujgawde/gridline/git/commits/d2a2a8db01e6eefbee782df48683f7b834af1eb5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87605577?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anujgawde","id":87605577,"login":"anujgawde","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NjA1NTc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anujgawde/gridline/commit/d2a2a8db01e6eefbee782df48683f7b834af1eb5","node_id":"C_kwDOUvi7UtoAKGQyYTJhOGRiMDFlNmVlZmJlZTc4MmRmNDg2ODNmN2I4MzRhZjFlYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anujgawde/gridline/commit/108754c4b53cea89414ba407fefe31246121ba94","sha":"108754c4b53cea89414ba407fefe31246121ba94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anujgawde/gridline/commits/108754c4b53cea89414ba407fefe31246121ba94"}],"sha":"d2a2a8db01e6eefbee782df48683f7b834af1eb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anujgawde/gridline/commits/d2a2a8db01e6eefbee782df48683f7b834af1eb5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87605577?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anujgawde","id":87605577,"login":"anujgawde","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NjA1NTc3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anujgawde","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anujgawde/gridline/commits/108754c4b53cea89414ba407fefe31246121ba94/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T23:09:51Z","email":"gawdeanuj@gmail.com","name":"anujgawde"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T23:09:51Z","email":"gawdeanuj@gmail.com","name":"anujgawde"},"message":"fix(viewer): keep sheet open inside the tile loader\n\nSheet open fetched its coarse tiles directly, bypassing the in-flight\ncap, the dedup and abortExcept — so it competed with the queue it was\ntrying to get ahead of, and its requests outlived a sheet change. A\ntile asked for by both paths was also decoded twice, and TileCache.set\ndropped the second decode without closing it. Those pixels sit outside\nthe JS heap, where the collector cannot reach them, and outside the\ncache''s byte total, where the budget cannot see them.\n\nAwaiting the loader needs to cover queued tiles as well as started\nones, since a tile behind the cap has no in-flight promise to await.","tree":{"sha":"c989150bd1b31154fbcfbbf005463125158a3270","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anujgawde/gridline/git/trees/c989150bd1b31154fbcfbbf005463125158a3270"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anujgawde/gridline/git/commits/108754c4b53cea89414ba407fefe31246121ba94","verification":{"pay