pi.github.com/users/DarksChoise/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarksChoise","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/code-corhuila/qone-front/commits/4dbf170d8488984f47c825c2e24920635595352c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T22:56:38Z","email":"86198522+DarksChoise@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Juan Diego Andrade Cardozo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T22:56:38Z","email":"86198522+DarksChoise@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Juan Diego Andrade Cardozo"},"message":"feat(auth): add RequireAuth, the development sign-in and the session routes\n\nRequireAuth guards every protected route: without a session the person\ngoes to /login carrying the requested route and returns to it after\nsigning in; because the session is React state (useSession over\nuseSyncExternalStore) a 401 that ends it redirects at once. DevSignIn\nimplements the development sign-in of norm 5.5.2 behind VITE_DEV_LOGIN\nwith the form rules of Annex H (label, error beside the field with\naria-describedby, button disabled while empty) and a data-testid the CI\ngrep uses to keep it out of main. The App gains /login and a protected\nhome; main.tsx restores the session at boot and starts the MSW worker\nwhen VITE_USE_MOCKS is true. The shell now exposes shell/apiClient and\nshell/session through Module Federation. Ten tests written first.\n\nRefs code-corhuila/qone-docs#37, code-corhuila/qone-docs#38","tree":{"sha":"96c7ea6c3ee68e5b5f34bc0f2b34ba9ae395c6a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/code-corhuila/qone-front/git/trees/96c7ea6c3ee68e5b5f34bc0f2b34ba9ae395c6a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/code-corhuila/qone-front/git/commits/4dbf170d8488984f47c825c2e24920635595352c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86198522?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/us