"https://api.github.com/users/DarksChoise/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarksChoise/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarksChoise/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarksChoise","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/code-corhuila/qone-catalog-portal/commits/4353ae04f1aff012c4475e4f438e0391d1423fcd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T00:17:50Z","email":"86198522+DarksChoise@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Juan Diego Andrade Cardozo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T00:17:50Z","email":"86198522+DarksChoise@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Juan Diego Andrade Cardozo"},"message":"feat(deploy): add the image, the NGINX config, the compose and the smoke checks of the remote\n\ndeploy/Dockerfile builds the remote with Node 22 and serves it with\nnginx:1.27-alpine; the only build argument is the shell origin.\ndeploy/nginx.conf serves remoteEntry.js and the chunks to any origin\n(CORS for GET), never caches remoteEntry.js, caches the hashed chunks\nfor a year, answers /health and has no SPA fallback because the portal\nhas no document of its own in the product. deploy/compose.yml is what\nqone-infra includes (platform network, PORTAL_PORT 5002 for develop).\ndeploy/smoke.sh checks health, the entry with its cache and CORS\nheaders, a referenced chunk and the 404 of unknown paths; ci.yml gains\nan image job that builds, runs and smoke-checks the container.\n\nRefs code-corhuila/qone-docs#35, code-corhuila/qone-docs#36","tree":{"sha":"45dcabfdb0be2f6d99364f88bebf38875cd099af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/code-corhuila/qone-catalog-portal/git/trees/45dcabfdb0be2f6d99364f88bebf38875cd099af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/code-corhuila/qone-catalog-portal/git/commits/4353ae04f1aff012c4475e4f438e0391d1423fcd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false