0:11:52Z","committedDate":"2026-09-29T00:11:52Z","committer":{"account":null,"email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:51:48.686Z","repositoryId":1394025233,"sha":"ebde085cb3bb780700b6a2554644f088f7df4f99"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:51:48.686Z","raw":[{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/5b529364af409c91eb16751e9beba144f5ddb1f4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T03:58:13Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T03:58:13Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: a refusal names its input and what is allowed; the body limit is configured and refused with its maximum\n\nImplements java-backend-api *A refusal names its input*, *A refused input gets one code wherever it travels*,\n*An undeclared member''s refusal lists the members allowed* and *A request body has a size limit, refused with its\nmaximum* (dulguun0225/skills 54604d5).\n\n- web::params: StrictPath, StrictQuery and StrictHeaders read what T''s IntoParams declares and refuse by `in` and\n  the declared `name`: validation.required (name absent), validation.invalid-value {expected} (blank, non-parsing,\n  a UUID in any but the 36-character form), validation.unknown-value {allowed}, validation.unknown-field {allowed}\n  for an undeclared query parameter on every route, validation.duplicate-member for a repeated one. axum''s Path and\n  Query banned outside web; validation.bad-request no longer answers a path variable that does not convert.\n- StrictJson: validation.unknown-field carries `allowed`, the members T declares, sorted; at most 100 entries\n  recorded, the rest counted as `errorsOmitted`.\n- REQUEST_BODY_MAX_BYTES (default 65,536, more than 0) replaces the BODY_LIMIT constant; the layer and the reader\n  both answer 413 request.too-large with `params.max`. Response codes declare params in wire_errors!; the snapshot\n  lists them, and an array param type carries `allowed`.\n- openapi/v1.json: an error entry is one of {pointer} or {in, name}; the problem declares `params` and\n  `errorsOmitted`; every operation declares its 400, every body-taking one its 413.\n- scripts/openapi.mjs: a breaking change made on purpose passes oasdiff only where a commit between the base and\n  HEAD declares each error-level finding in an `OpenAPI-break: <id> <METHOD> <path>` trailer; the declaration\n  covers this change alone, since the next base is past it. Its judge runs canaries every time. For a document no\n  consumer binds yet; a released one crossing the build boundary takes a new major version. GATES.md row and a\n  named gap for that limit; CLAUDE.md says how.\n\nThe error-entry change below is breaking for oasdiff: adding `oneOf` to the `errors` items of every problem\nresponse. This template''s document has no consumer; a service porting it treats it as its own breaking change.\n\nOpenAPI-break: response-property-one-of-added POST /api/greetings\nOpenAPI-break: response-property-one-of-added GET /api/greetings/{id}\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dcc5259b6eeab2b23de05b010aee85c937c4ed2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/dcc5259b6eeab2b23de05b010aee85c937c4ed2e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/5b529364af409c91eb16751e9beba144f5ddb1f4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/5b529364af409c91eb16751e9beba144f5ddb1f4","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKDViNTI5MzY0YWY0MDljOTFlYjE2NzUxZTliZWJhMTQ0ZjVkZGIxZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/b6e9f071355e7686aaf9eb75110a7f52596aef9c","sha":"b6e9f071355e7686aaf9eb75110a7f52596aef9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/b6e9f071355e7686aaf9eb75110a7f52596aef9c"}],"sha":"5b529364af409c91eb16751e9beba144f5ddb1f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/5b529364af409c91eb16751e9beba144f5ddb1f4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/b6e9f071355e7686aaf9eb75110a7f52596aef9c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:19:54Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:19:54Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: the lock canary runs the check''s own command, online; offline it needed a warm cargo index and failed on a cold runner\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6e004312954512b49ed1bdbec505551ad410de74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/6e004312954512b49ed1bdbec505551ad410de74"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/b6e9f071355e7686aaf9eb75110a7f52596aef9c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/b6e9f071355e7686aaf9eb75110a7f52596aef9c","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKGI2ZTlmMDcxMzU1ZTc2ODZhYWY5ZWI3NTExMGE3ZjUyNTk2YWVmOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/4bb47f493e8c1002eedbe12b772e7dce3aebd353","sha":"4bb47f493e8c1002eedbe12b772e7dce3aebd353","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/4bb47f493e8c1002eedbe12b772e7dce3aebd353"}],"sha":"b6e9f071355e7686aaf9eb75110a7f52596aef9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/b6e9f071355e7686aaf9eb75110a7f52596aef9c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/4bb47f493e8c1002eedbe12b772e7dce3aebd353/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:12:16Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:12:16Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"deps: move yoke-derive 0.8.3 to 0.8.4; 0.8.3 is yanked and cargo-deny refuses a yanked version\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b4338368c25acd06b8f471a9d4f9f390740f10f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/b4338368c25acd06b8f471a9d4f9f390740f10f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/4bb47f493e8c1002eedbe12b772e7dce3aebd353","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/4bb47f493e8c1002eedbe12b772e7dce3aebd353","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKDRiYjQ3ZjQ5M2U4YzEwMDJlZWRiZTEyYjc3MmU3ZGNlM2FlYmQzNTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/626180dc93b6b587ecd366e76d7b7cb42acf3647","sha":"626180dc93b6b587ecd366e76d7b7cb42acf3647","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/626180dc93b6b587ecd366e76d7b7cb42acf3647"}],"sha":"4bb47f493e8c1002eedbe12b772e7dce3aebd353","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/4bb47f493e8c1002eedbe12b772e7dce3aebd353"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/626180dc93b6b587ecd366e76d7b7cb42acf3647/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T01:56:36Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T01:56:36Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: a duplicate member is refused at any depth; a field code declares its params, carried in the entry\n\nThe body reader recorded a repeated top-level member, but read each member''s value as a serde_json::Value,\nwhich keeps one of two values of a repeated nested member silently. It now reads values itself and records\nthe pointer of every repeated member at any depth as validation.duplicate-member, before any value is built,\nin the one reader every body passes. The other two ways a repetition collapses, a map-typed member and\nflatten, were already refused: the request-body contract holds members to scalars and the serde source rules\nban flatten. The strict-body sweep sends each member twice and each member as an object repeating a member,\nthrough every documented body-taking operation.\n\nfield_codes! takes a variant''s params as its fields, `TooLong { max: u16 } = \"validation.too-long\"`, each an\ninteger type or a &''static str, so a code that declares params does not compile without them (E0533). The\nfield error carries them as `params`, `{\"max\": 100}`, absent when the code declares none; its fields are\nprivate to web, so no other crate writes a code or a param list by hand. The catalog snapshot lists each\nfield code''s params with their JSON types; one wire code declares one param list across catalogs, and a\nparam name is one lower-case word, being its wire name. validation.wrong-type declares `expected`;\nvalidation.too-long declares `max`, and NAME_MAX_CHARS is a u16. The OpenAPI document gains the optional\n`params` member, a non-breaking change by oasdiff.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"47251af8bd629f1f66575363f666a0380273fa71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/47251af8bd629f1f66575363f666a0380273fa71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/626180dc93b6b587ecd366e76d7b7cb42acf3647","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/626180dc93b6b587ecd366e76d7b7cb42acf3647","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKDYyNjE4MGRjOTNiNmI1ODdlY2QzNjZlNzZkN2I3Y2I0MmFjZjM2NDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/aacc689a9bb53fb45974fc63c8f1e0a8bb882366","sha":"aacc689a9bb53fb45974fc63c8f1e0a8bb882366","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/aacc689a9bb53fb45974fc63c8f1e0a8bb882366"}],"sha":"626180dc93b6b587ecd366e76d7b7cb42acf3647","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/626180dc93b6b587ecd366e76d7b7cb42acf3647"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/aacc689a9bb53fb45974fc63c8f1e0a8bb882366/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T01:56:36Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T01:56:36Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"scaffold: move the runtime base image digest; libssl3t64 3.5.7-1~deb13u2 carried two HIGH CVEs\n\nThe wall''s image scan refused gcr.io/distroless/cc-debian13:nonroot@sha256:54df941e…: CVE-2026-75804 and\nCVE-2026-84782 in libssl3t64 3.5.7-1~deb13u2, fixed in deb13u3. The tag''s current digest, e792ab3d…, scans\nclean with trivy 0.74.0, and the wall''s image step passes over it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cd6a8eaf14119c4c7d50f6e566bd1e7c286745b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/cd6a8eaf14119c4c7d50f6e566bd1e7c286745b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/aacc689a9bb53fb45974fc63c8f1e0a8bb882366","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/aacc689a9bb53fb45974fc63c8f1e0a8bb882366","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKGFhY2M2ODlhOWJiNTNmYjQ1OTc0ZmM2M2M4ZjFlMGE4YmI4ODIzNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/5cdc93a004ebe28fcba1d02a2a554eaaf6c75e97","sha":"5cdc93a004ebe28fcba1d02a2a554eaaf6c75e97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/5cdc93a004ebe28fcba1d02a2a554eaaf6c75e97"}],"sha":"aacc689a9bb53fb45974fc63c8f1e0a8bb882366","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/aacc689a9bb53fb45974fc63c8f1e0a8bb882366"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/5cdc93a004ebe28fcba1d02a2a554eaaf6c75e97/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T04:19:05Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T04:19:05Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: every mise tool pinned by checksum in mise.lock; the wall refuses a stale lock or a missing checksum\n\nmise.lock beside mise.toml and project-root/mise.toml, written with mise 2026.9.7 in lock format 2, which\n2026.9.7, 2026.9.15 and the pinned 2026.9.16 read (a new lock from 2026.9.16 is format 3, which 2026.9.15\nrejects), with a url and sha256 for linux-x64, linux-arm64, macos-x64, macos-arm64 and windows-x64; its\nchecksums and urls equal those of a separate 2026.9.16 run. mise.toml sets [tool_config] locked = true, so\nmise install refuses a tool the lock lacks instead of rewriting the lock, and lockfile_platforms, so\nmise lock refreshes all five.\n\nscripts/check-mise-lock.mjs runs first in the wall: a tool at a version or options the lock lacks, a lock\nentry mise.toml does not list, a platform without a url or accepted checksum, a missing lock, locked or\nlockfile_platforms unset, and a declared exemption that no longer applies each fail; fixtures under\nscripts/fixtures/mise-lock show each refused by its rule alone. Declared exemptions, each a named gap:\ncargo:sqlx-cli, built from source, and cargo-mutants on arm64, which has no release build. By hand with\nmise 2026.9.16: a changed digit in trivy''s linux-x64 sha256 failed mise install, exit 1.\n\nThe suppression inventory hashes mise.lock, so an edit to it is listed; a Renovate PR moving a mise pin\ncarries the lock (Renovate''s mise manager runs `mise lock <tool>`, read from its source) and needs\ncheck-suppressions --write pushed to it. GitLab''s mise cache keys on mise.lock.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"320346e2fa7041e56e29883e7c369a5f4b54150f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/320346e2fa7041e56e29883e7c369a5f4b54150f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/5cdc93a004ebe28fcba1d02a2a554eaaf6c75e97","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/5cdc93a004ebe28fcba1d02a2a554eaaf6c75e97","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKDVjZGM5M2EwMDRlYmUyOGZjYmExZDAyYTJhNTU0ZWFhZjZjNzVlOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/c5a25907efb2e4ceb376b19374c7952d6705dea8","sha":"c5a25907efb2e4ceb376b19374c7952d6705dea8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/c5a25907efb2e4ceb376b19374c7952d6705dea8"}],"sha":"5cdc93a004ebe28fcba1d02a2a554eaaf6c75e97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/5cdc93a004ebe28fcba1d02a2a554eaaf6c75e97"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/c5a25907efb2e4ceb376b19374c7952d6705dea8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T03:00:58Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T03:00:58Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: scan the service image with trivy; HIGH and CRITICAL fail, fixed or not\n\nThe wall builds the Dockerfile''s image as <binary>:wall and runs trivy 0.74.0 (mise.toml) over its packages.\nAn unfixed HIGH or CRITICAL fails too: it is exposed all the same, and --ignore-unfixed would hide it with no\nrecord. The one exception is a .trivyignore entry with its reason and an expiry, each listed in\nsuppressions.txt. Canary, every run: the Dockerfile''s final base plus a dpkg record for openssl 3.5.1-1 must\nbe refused, pass with its findings ignored, and be refused again with the entries expired. trivy reads no\nTRIVY_* variable but the cache directory and no trivy.yaml. CI caches the database per UTC day. The image\nscan leaves GATES'' Not reached; the image''s package licences and the database''s integrity are named there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d4626602c4ded48f01d54d895d30ed697aa07b30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/d4626602c4ded48f01d54d895d30ed697aa07b30"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/c5a25907efb2e4ceb376b19374c7952d6705dea8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/c5a25907efb2e4ceb376b19374c7952d6705dea8","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKGM1YTI1OTA3ZWZiMmU0Y2ViMzc2YjE5Mzc0Yzc5NTJkNjcwNWRlYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/c7e4ce213431dae1ea61791729ab6786c66c77bf","sha":"c7e4ce213431dae1ea61791729ab6786c66c77bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/c7e4ce213431dae1ea61791729ab6786c66c77bf"}],"sha":"c5a25907efb2e4ceb376b19374c7952d6705dea8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/c5a25907efb2e4ceb376b19374c7952d6705dea8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/c7e4ce213431dae1ea61791729ab6786c66c77bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:10:50Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:10:50Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: refuse `$n IS NULL OR …` in a checked query\n\nThe optional-parameter predicate the pager''s worked example used is a filter under a generic plan, so a keyset\nseek written that way reads every row before its page. check-sql refuses it with a fixture; the previous\nworked example''s statement is refused.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b64c770e9f1f7a9a381dd905c45c68417833eb37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/b64c770e9f1f7a9a381dd905c45c68417833eb37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/c7e4ce213431dae1ea61791729ab6786c66c77bf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/c7e4ce213431dae1ea61791729ab6786c66c77bf","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKGM3ZTRjZTIxMzQzMWRhZTFlYTYxNzkxNzI5YWI2Nzg2YzY2Yzc3YmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/ba07939fdc96e75d0b502901819a7ec0c4f2315b","sha":"ba07939fdc96e75d0b502901819a7ec0c4f2315b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/ba07939fdc96e75d0b502901819a7ec0c4f2315b"}],"sha":"c7e4ce213431dae1ea61791729ab6786c66c77bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/c7e4ce213431dae1ea61791729ab6786c66c77bf"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/ba07939fdc96e75d0b502901819a7ec0c4f2315b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:10:50Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:10:50Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"scaffold: the pager''s keyset seek is an index condition under a generic plan\n\nstore::greeting::page ran one statement with `$1::timestamptz is null or (created_at, id) < ($1, $2)`. Under\na generic plan, which PostgreSQL may choose for a prepared statement after five runs, that is a filter, not an\nindex condition: a page near the end of 200,000 rows removed 199,990 by the filter, the cost OFFSET has. The\nfirst page and the pages after a cursor are now two statements; the second reads 4 buffers under a generic\nplan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1b1def802f5398d270e6a126ccf384ad726f03e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/1b1def802f5398d270e6a126ccf384ad726f03e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/ba07939fdc96e75d0b502901819a7ec0c4f2315b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/ba07939fdc96e75d0b502901819a7ec0c4f2315b","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKGJhMDc5MzlmZGM5NmU3NWQwYjUwMjkwMTgxOWE3ZWMwYzRmMjMxNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/340af7e4b3f9e32651cd37e32f1cb7d99c9146dc","sha":"340af7e4b3f9e32651cd37e32f1cb7d99c9146dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/340af7e4b3f9e32651cd37e32f1cb7d99c9146dc"}],"sha":"ba07939fdc96e75d0b502901819a7ec0c4f2315b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/ba07939fdc96e75d0b502901819a7ec0c4f2315b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/340af7e4b3f9e32651cd37e32f1cb7d99c9146dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:07:26Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:07:26Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: refuse a crate-local rustfmt.toml and switched-off test targets; list ignore and rustfmt::skip\n\ndisable_all_formatting = true in crates/api/rustfmt.toml passed cargo fmt --check over an unformatted\nfunction: rustfmt reads the nearest configuration. A target with test = false or harness = false, or\nautotests = false, drops tests with no test file changing. Both are refused with fixtures; #[ignore] and\n#[rustfmt::skip] now appear in the suppression inventory beside allow and expect.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"590423ee61f9b4af6b1b1ef6b35573a1d46b29cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/590423ee61f9b4af6b1b1ef6b35573a1d46b29cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/340af7e4b3f9e32651cd37e32f1cb7d99c9146dc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/340af7e4b3f9e32651cd37e32f1cb7d99c9146dc","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKDM0MGFmN2U0YjNmOWUzMjY1MWNkMzdlMzJmMWNiN2Q5OWM5MTQ2ZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/fdb364c0de2618755e5c7940c48614fe85a370c8","sha":"fdb364c0de2618755e5c7940c48614fe85a370c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/fdb364c0de2618755e5c7940c48614fe85a370c8"}],"sha":"340af7e4b3f9e32651cd37e32f1cb7d99c9146dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/340af7e4b3f9e32651cd37e32f1cb7d99c9146dc"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/fdb364c0de2618755e5c7940c48614fe85a370c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:11Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:11Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"docs: GATES, README and CLAUDE.md match the gates\n\nGATES: every new rule, ban and step with what shows it failing; Not reached gains the routes this review\nfound and left, the container image scan, and the guardrails-toolchain steps the project owns. README: the\ntemplate''s GitHub workflow ran green on e230ed9; gitleaks among the tools. CLAUDE.md: api declares sqlx as a\ndev-dependency; the constructs the wall now refuses.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a05812594e803573dd8e1cb8f0b589472b6753c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/a05812594e803573dd8e1cb8f0b589472b6753c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/fdb364c0de2618755e5c7940c48614fe85a370c8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/fdb364c0de2618755e5c7940c48614fe85a370c8","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKGZkYjM2NGMwZGUyNjE4NzU1ZTVjNzk0MGM0ODYxNGZlODVhMzcwYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/e89c8683d008ccdf832a938e44a6ae27c08225a5","sha":"e89c8683d008ccdf832a938e44a6ae27c08225a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/e89c8683d008ccdf832a938e44a6ae27c08225a5"}],"sha":"fdb364c0de2618755e5c7940c48614fe85a370c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/fdb364c0de2618755e5c7940c48614fe85a370c8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/e89c8683d008ccdf832a938e44a6ae27c08225a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:11Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:11Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"scaffold: init refuses a Windows device name\n\nA binary named con or nul cannot be written on Windows, where the scripts claim to run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"609e0358af75937d0bf2f8c37f15bd4dc05c7b5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/609e0358af75937d0bf2f8c37f15bd4dc05c7b5e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/e89c8683d008ccdf832a938e44a6ae27c08225a5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/e89c8683d008ccdf832a938e44a6ae27c08225a5","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKGU4OWM4NjgzZDAwOGNjZGY4MzJhOTM4ZTQ0YTZhZTI3YzA4MjI1YTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/e7e9d7d52a1b183f6fd5ae6bf2268f2519482221","sha":"e7e9d7d52a1b183f6fd5ae6bf2268f2519482221","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/e7e9d7d52a1b183f6fd5ae6bf2268f2519482221"}],"sha":"e89c8683d008ccdf832a938e44a6ae27c08225a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/e89c8683d008ccdf832a938e44a6ae27c08225a5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/e7e9d7d52a1b183f6fd5ae6bf2268f2519482221/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:11Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:11Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"scaffold: time declares the macros feature platform''s tests use\n\ncargo test -p platform failed to compile: time''s macros feature came only from another crate in a\nworkspace build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9edc26468224a666847b6806973656cabfcddc8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/9edc26468224a666847b6806973656cabfcddc8e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/e7e9d7d52a1b183f6fd5ae6bf2268f2519482221","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/e7e9d7d52a1b183f6fd5ae6bf2268f2519482221","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKGU3ZTlkN2Q1MmExYjE4M2Y2ZmQ1YWU2YmYyMjY4ZjI1MTk0ODIyMjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/9e5246858995d73cdfaa8c6b20c8a6cc0aa7ea39","sha":"9e5246858995d73cdfaa8c6b20c8a6cc0aa7ea39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/9e5246858995d73cdfaa8c6b20c8a6cc0aa7ea39"}],"sha":"e7e9d7d52a1b183f6fd5ae6bf2268f2519482221","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/e7e9d7d52a1b183f6fd5ae6bf2268f2519482221"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/9e5246858995d73cdfaa8c6b20c8a6cc0aa7ea39/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:10Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:10Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"scaffold: the API log capture no longer races tracing''s call-site cache\n\nWith one dispatcher registered, tracing computes a call site''s interest from the registering thread''s own\ndefault, so a parallel test with no capture cached never and the capturing test missed its event in 3 of\n100 runs. A global subscriber that asks at every call site keeps a second dispatcher registered: 0 of 200.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ba5cf6fce3c91cf51011ddb50a41b3a33e5a34cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/ba5cf6fce3c91cf51011ddb50a41b3a33e5a34cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/9e5246858995d73cdfaa8c6b20c8a6cc0aa7ea39","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/9e5246858995d73cdfaa8c6b20c8a6cc0aa7ea39","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKDllNTI0Njg1ODk5NWQ3M2NkZmFhOGM2YjIwYzhhNmNjMGFhN2VhMzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/3fbf64e3fe7aa449cb0584e8810ceef545504c3a","sha":"3fbf64e3fe7aa449cb0584e8810ceef545504c3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/3fbf64e3fe7aa449cb0584e8810ceef545504c3a"}],"sha":"9e5246858995d73cdfaa8c6b20c8a6cc0aa7ea39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/9e5246858995d73cdfaa8c6b20c8a6cc0aa7ea39"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/3fbf64e3fe7aa449cb0584e8810ceef545504c3a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:10Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:10Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"scaffold: the page limit is a NonZeroU16\n\nto_page with a zero limit returned an empty page and no cursor while rows remained, which ends a client''s\nwalk of the list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9bb5684c592f1b7b28ac34e89083a7cfbb571ec2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/9bb5684c592f1b7b28ac34e89083a7cfbb571ec2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/3fbf64e3fe7aa449cb0584e8810ceef545504c3a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/3fbf64e3fe7aa449cb0584e8810ceef545504c3a","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKDNmYmY2NGUzZmU3YWE0NDljYjA1ODRlODgxMGNlZWY1NDU1MDRjM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/a3db78b0fb3a905f51a6a83d2ca0693436fc2dc8","sha":"a3db78b0fb3a905f51a6a83d2ca0693436fc2dc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/a3db78b0fb3a905f51a6a83d2ca0693436fc2dc8"}],"sha":"3fbf64e3fe7aa449cb0584e8810ceef545504c3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/3fbf64e3fe7aa449cb0584e8810ceef545504c3a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/a3db78b0fb3a905f51a6a83d2ca0693436fc2dc8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:10Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:10Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: the action-pin check reads flow-style uses and runs a selftest in CI\n\n- { uses: actions/checkout@v7 } passed the check, and nothing showed the check failing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9cc945511dac561a724e304c1d307e272e5766c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/9cc945511dac561a724e304c1d307e272e5766c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/a3db78b0fb3a905f51a6a83d2ca0693436fc2dc8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/a3db78b0fb3a905f51a6a83d2ca0693436fc2dc8","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKGEzZGI3OGIwZmIzYTkwNWY1MWE2YTgzZDJjYTA2OTM0MzZmYzJkYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/9ca52a8fafbf25dcba2d77a088130eabc66cb0dd","sha":"9ca52a8fafbf25dcba2d77a088130eabc66cb0dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/9ca52a8fafbf25dcba2d77a088130eabc66cb0dd"}],"sha":"a3db78b0fb3a905f51a6a83d2ca0693436fc2dc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/a3db78b0fb3a905f51a6a83d2ca0693436fc2dc8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/9ca52a8fafbf25dcba2d77a088130eabc66cb0dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:10Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:10Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: the inventory hashes the gates'' own scripts, fixtures and canaries\n\nIt claimed every file that decides what a gate refuses; the scripts (the coverage floors among them), the\nfixture trees, the canaries and the profile tables other than [profile.release] were not hashed. A digest\nRenovate moves inside a script is masked.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7d26023c449a503902fa7d2f3c3539718c9b2f9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/7d26023c449a503902fa7d2f3c3539718c9b2f9f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/9ca52a8fafbf25dcba2d77a088130eabc66cb0dd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/9ca52a8fafbf25dcba2d77a088130eabc66cb0dd","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKDljYTUyYThmYWZiZjI1ZGNiYTJkNzdhMDg4MTMwZWFiYzY2Y2IwZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/916541520567b6444da3cab385f072f2f2ec7bb7","sha":"916541520567b6444da3cab385f072f2f2ec7bb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/916541520567b6444da3cab385f072f2f2ec7bb7"}],"sha":"9ca52a8fafbf25dcba2d77a088130eabc66cb0dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/9ca52a8fafbf25dcba2d77a088130eabc66cb0dd"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/916541520567b6444da3cab385f072f2f2ec7bb7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:10Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:10Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: the wall checks Cargo.lock first, refuses any clippy warning, and scans for secrets\n\ncargo-deny, run without --locked, rewrote a stale Cargo.lock, and every --locked step after it passed over a\nlock the commit lacked; cargo metadata --locked now runs first, with a canary, and cargo-deny runs --locked.\n#![warn(warnings)] with #![warn(clippy::disallowed_methods)] exited 0 printing a warning; any clippy warning\nnow fails the wall. gitleaks 8.30.1 scans the files git would commit and, given a base, the commits since\nit, with a generated configuration and --ignore-gitleaks-allow; its canaries are a token marked\ngitleaks:allow and a token added and removed inside one range.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0247c741d9937c0d33291dcaae198fbec4467c3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/0247c741d9937c0d33291dcaae198fbec4467c3d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/916541520567b6444da3cab385f072f2f2ec7bb7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/916541520567b6444da3cab385f072f2f2ec7bb7","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKDkxNjU0MTUyMDU2N2I2NDQ0ZGEzY2FiMzg1ZjA3MmYyZjJlYzdiYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/205ac3e05b4301f95ad37c38eb709640e51f8458","sha":"205ac3e05b4301f95ad37c38eb709640e51f8458","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/205ac3e05b4301f95ad37c38eb709640e51f8458"}],"sha":"916541520567b6444da3cab385f072f2f2ec7bb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/916541520567b6444da3cab385f072f2f2ec7bb7"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/205ac3e05b4301f95ad37c38eb709640e51f8458/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:10Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:10Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: refuse a renamed Deserialize\n\nuse serde::Deserialize as Lenient; #[derive(Lenient)] hid the derive from all three serde rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"00daebe74387194e58ec6174615888ca277c01ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/00daebe74387194e58ec6174615888ca277c01ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/205ac3e05b4301f95ad37c38eb709640e51f8458","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/205ac3e05b4301f95ad37c38eb709640e51f8458","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKDIwNWFjM2UwNWI0MzAxZjk1YWQzN2MzOGViNzA5NjQwZTUxZjg0NTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/ee3e15c0828ab76fbe1efdffb68135ed26149265","sha":"ee3e15c0828ab76fbe1efdffb68135ed26149265","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/ee3e15c0828ab76fbe1efdffb68135ed26149265"}],"sha":"205ac3e05b4301f95ad37c38eb709640e51f8458","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/205ac3e05b4301f95ad37c38eb709640e51f8458"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/ee3e15c0828ab76fbe1efdffb68135ed26149265/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:10Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:10Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: SQL and migration rules read quoted and qualified names, every money column and SQL clocks\n\nEach passed before: update \"greeting\" and update public.greeting without the version guard; an insert into\n\"audit\" from crates/api; a write in crates/store/src/lib.rs, outside any feature; order by \"id\";\n''now''::timestamptz; gen_random_uuid() and uuidv7() in a query; create table \"orders\" with no owner; a\nmoney column declared on one line, added by alter table, or quoted. New rules id-in-sql and\nwrite-outside-feature; fixtures may carry variants.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6fff5830a6618589ac90bbf7f66eabf9ebfa6894","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/6fff5830a6618589ac90bbf7f66eabf9ebfa6894"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/ee3e15c0828ab76fbe1efdffb68135ed26149265","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/ee3e15c0828ab76fbe1efdffb68135ed26149265","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKGVlM2UxNWMwODI4YWI3NmZiZTFlZmRmZmI2ODEzNWVkMjYxNDkyNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/7c7eca7a9feeb1249ef6790f10f8e8ebe625ee3a","sha":"7c7eca7a9feeb1249ef6790f10f8e8ebe625ee3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/7c7eca7a9feeb1249ef6790f10f8e8ebe625ee3a"}],"sha":"ee3e15c0828ab76fbe1efdffb68135ed26149265","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/ee3e15c0828ab76fbe1efdffb68135ed26149265"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/7c7eca7a9feeb1249ef6790f10f8e8ebe625ee3a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:09Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:09Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: ban pool creation outside db, the remaining clock reads, uuid::Builder and blocking std::fs\n\nA store function built PgPool::connect_lazy(url) and ran query_scalar!(…).fetch_optional(&pool) outside\nany transaction, green. The connect* methods of Pool, PoolOptions and Connection are banned outside db,\nwhich keeps PoolOptions::connect. SystemTime::elapsed and uuid::Timestamp::now read the wall clock;\nuuid::Builder makes an id without the producer; hard_link, read_link, set_permissions, File::create_new\nand DirBuilder::create block. Each ban has its canary line.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"84c7249632ced9d3b76850ceadc35e1d35331b50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/84c7249632ced9d3b76850ceadc35e1d35331b50"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/7c7eca7a9feeb1249ef6790f10f8e8ebe625ee3a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/7c7eca7a9feeb1249ef6790f10f8e8ebe625ee3a","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKDdjN2VjYTdhOWZlZWIxMjQ5ZWY2NzkwZjEwZjhlOGViZTYyNWVlM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/dc3651469ab11cb9a31cc22b25184986caddcfae","sha":"dc3651469ab11cb9a31cc22b25184986caddcfae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/dc3651469ab11cb9a31cc22b25184986caddcfae"}],"sha":"7c7eca7a9feeb1249ef6790f10f8e8ebe625ee3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/7c7eca7a9feeb1249ef6790f10f8e8ebe625ee3a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/dc3651469ab11cb9a31cc22b25184986caddcfae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:09Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T02:05:09Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: refuse the routes that built banned code with every check green\n\nOn a scaffolded service each of these compiled a banned call or shipped a release build without a guard,\nwith clippy, check-lint-config and the suppression inventory all passing: #[warn] lowering a denied lint\n(and #![warn(warnings)]); a renamed lint name behind an expect of renamed_and_removed_lints; a lint name\nfrom a macro variable; #[path] to a .txt file and include!; cfg(not(debug_assertions)), a negated feature\nand cfg(coverage), which clippy on the dev profile with every feature never reads; a build script setting\na release-only cfg; a path dependency on a crate outside the workspace; overflow-checks = false in a\npackage override, a cargo config or CARGO_PROFILE_*; CARGO_BUILD_RUSTFLAGS and cargo --config in the\nDockerfile; a project root''s .cargo/config.toml. Each is now a rule with a fixture, fixtures may carry\nvariants and mark the lines that must be refused, and fixture members moved to crates/member.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0d19e4412066e53cd9e8414c00c2789cf0ac23e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/0d19e4412066e53cd9e8414c00c2789cf0ac23e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/dc3651469ab11cb9a31cc22b25184986caddcfae","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/dc3651469ab11cb9a31cc22b25184986caddcfae","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKGRjMzY1MTQ2OWFiMTFjYjlhMzFjYzIyYjI1MTg0OTg2Y2FkZGNmYWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/e230ed905a0a753d04ba911289009006a69a103c","sha":"e230ed905a0a753d04ba911289009006a69a103c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/e230ed905a0a753d04ba911289009006a69a103c"}],"sha":"dc3651469ab11cb9a31cc22b25184986caddcfae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/dc3651469ab11cb9a31cc22b25184986caddcfae"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/e230ed905a0a753d04ba911289009006a69a103c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T00:57:34Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T00:57:34Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"docs: README, CLAUDE.md and GATES.md\n\nGATES.md maps each wired gate to the record section or skill directive\nit implements and to what shows it failing, records the runs the stack\nrecord owed, the deviations from it, and what no gate here reaches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9cfe4114a6ece90a65d58fc7d21f7e9d10432fc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/9cfe4114a6ece90a65d58fc7d21f7e9d10432fc1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/e230ed905a0a753d04ba911289009006a69a103c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/e230ed905a0a753d04ba911289009006a69a103c","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKGUyMzBlZDkwNWEwYTc1M2QwNGJhOTExMjg5MDA5MDA2YTY5YTEwM2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/2507581d0d92c3ed238568545f406d3b9628ea4a","sha":"2507581d0d92c3ed238568545f406d3b9628ea4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/2507581d0d92c3ed238568545f406d3b9628ea4a"}],"sha":"e230ed905a0a753d04ba911289009006a69a103c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/e230ed905a0a753d04ba911289009006a69a103c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/2507581d0d92c3ed238568545f406d3b9628ea4a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T00:57:34Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T00:57:34Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"scaffold: init.mjs checks every edit, the base-branch move included, before writing any\n\nA standalone run renamed five files and then stopped on a missing\nCLAUDE.md, leaving a half-renamed tree. Every target of the run is now\nread and matched first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0d87597a20beb731412f6d90c1027348919cabe6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/0d87597a20beb731412f6d90c1027348919cabe6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/2507581d0d92c3ed238568545f406d3b9628ea4a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/2507581d0d92c3ed238568545f406d3b9628ea4a","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKDI1MDc1ODFkMGQ5MmMzZWQyMzg1Njg1NDVmNDA2ZDNiOTYyOGVhNGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/513e9e25e1c73963c2afa15f9fe9e14398febb85","sha":"513e9e25e1c73963c2afa15f9fe9e14398febb85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/513e9e25e1c73963c2afa15f9fe9e14398febb85"}],"sha":"2507581d0d92c3ed238568545f406d3b9628ea4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/2507581d0d92c3ed238568545f406d3b9628ea4a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/513e9e25e1c73963c2afa15f9fe9e14398febb85/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T00:54:37Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T00:54:37Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: tests that kill every surviving mutant; vendored paths for the base-branch checks\n\nA full cargo-mutants pass over the workspace left 22 mutants alive. Each\nis now killed: tests for Money''s sign and zero, the 19- and 20-digit\nboundary in DbAmount, a nullable request member, an exact-length name,\nthe captured log text and the shutdown future; mul_div_round reads the\nsign with is_negative and is_positive, where a comparison with zero could\nnot be told from its mutant; the reader''s detail and the edge''s status\nmap lose arms no input reaches. The last whole-workspace pass ended at\nexit 3 with one timeout and no miss.\n\nAn exact tie is now built by a property of its own: the HalfEven mutant\npassed the random-input properties, where ties are rare. An absent Option\nmember marked deserialize_with is validation.required at its pointer. A\nbody over BODY_LIMIT read by an extractor with a larger limit of its own\nis 413. The base-branch checks read paths relative to the service\ndirectory, so they work vendored as backend/.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c9eaa2d0c715c1cc47b22c1de7c3e6186567224b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/c9eaa2d0c715c1cc47b22c1de7c3e6186567224b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/513e9e25e1c73963c2afa15f9fe9e14398febb85","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/513e9e25e1c73963c2afa15f9fe9e14398febb85","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKDUxM2U5ZTI1ZTFjNzM5NjNjMmFmYTE1ZjlmZTllMTQzOThmZWJiODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/2b3ea8672d9e71d359c9cd68af9b747c4cf2e43c","sha":"2b3ea8672d9e71d359c9cd68af9b747c4cf2e43c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/2b3ea8672d9e71d359c9cd68af9b747c4cf2e43c"}],"sha":"513e9e25e1c73963c2afa15f9fe9e14398febb85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/513e9e25e1c73963c2afa15f9fe9e14398febb85"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/2b3ea8672d9e71d359c9cd68af9b747c4cf2e43c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T00:54:37Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T00:54:37Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"scaffold: project root, init.mjs, CI workflows and Renovate\n\nproject-root/ carries what a project needs at its root, as in\njava-backend-template: CI with backend and frontend jobs (the backend job\nruns mise in backend/), the dev and main rulesets and their scripts, a\nGitLab mirror, compose on PostgreSQL 18.6, the frontend stub and the\nproject CLAUDE.md. scripts/init.mjs --name <name> [--standalone] is the\nonly rename step: it validates the name as a crate-name-safe identifier,\nrenames the binary, the document title, the image and the local database,\nand in vendored mode lifts project-root/ one level up without overwriting.\nThe lint-configuration guard also scans a vendored project''s root CI,\ncompose, mise and script files, and the wall''s database is reachable\nthrough WALL_DB_HOST on docker:dind.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a6e9e8c3d00c290db9a433cfdf577e3b629b5afb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/a6e9e8c3d00c290db9a433cfdf577e3b629b5afb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/2b3ea8672d9e71d359c9cd68af9b747c4cf2e43c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/2b3ea8672d9e71d359c9cd68af9b747c4cf2e43c","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKDJiM2VhODY3MmQ5ZTcxZDM1OWM5Y2Q2OGFmOWI3NDdjNGNmMmU0M2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/485c12f612aa464f567ac4a8917da14686aca927","sha":"485c12f612aa464f567ac4a8917da14686aca927","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/485c12f612aa464f567ac4a8917da14686aca927"}],"sha":"2b3ea8672d9e71d359c9cd68af9b747c4cf2e43c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/2b3ea8672d9e71d359c9cd68af9b747c4cf2e43c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/485c12f612aa464f567ac4a8917da14686aca927/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T00:31:17Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T00:31:17Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: every gate of the Rust stack record, each with the canary that shows it failing\n\nscripts/wall.mjs is the definition of done. It runs, in order: the lint\nconfiguration guards (cap-lints, flag overrides, rustflags, lints\ninheritance, cfg(clippy), suppressed ban lints, allow-invalid, generated\nclippy scopes, overflow-checks, panic mode, exact toolchain); the\nsuppression inventory; rustfmt and the ast-grep serde rules; the SQL\nrules (table ownership, guarded version update, ORDER BY id, OFFSET,\nSQL clock); migration conventions, applied-migration immutability and\nsquawk; crate-graph layering, cargo-deny and cargo-shear; then, on a\nthrowaway PostgreSQL 18.6, the sqlx prepare check, clippy, the ban\ncanaries, the tests under cargo-llvm-cov floors, the OpenAPI rerun,\nvacuum and oasdiff, and cargo-mutants over the diff.\n\nEvery script-hosted gate runs its negative fixture or canary first and\nfails when the canary passes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"95c00dc4cdece41f2efebe3c549c5e064b7c9c8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/95c00dc4cdece41f2efebe3c549c5e064b7c9c8a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/485c12f612aa464f567ac4a8917da14686aca927","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/485c12f612aa464f567ac4a8917da14686aca927","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKDQ4NWMxMmY2MTJhYTQ2NGY1NjdhYzRhODkxN2RhMTQ2ODZhY2E5Mjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/ebde085cb3bb780700b6a2554644f088f7df4f99","sha":"ebde085cb3bb780700b6a2554644f088f7df4f99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/ebde085cb3bb780700b6a2554644f088f7df4f99"}],"sha":"485c12f612aa464f567ac4a8917da14686aca927","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/485c12f612aa464f567ac4a8917da14686aca927"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/ebde085cb3bb780700b6a2554644f088f7df4f99/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T00:11:52Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T00:11:52Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"scaffold: Rust service workspace on axum, sqlx and PostgreSQL 18\n\nOne crate per layer: platform (clock, UUIDv7 ids, the typed logging\nfacade, the wire-code catalogs, the keyset pager), money (whole minor\nunits and mul_div_round), money-sql (the one NUMERIC mapper), db (the\nmigrator and Tx, the one transaction seam), store (feature SQL, checked\nmacros only), web (RFC 9457 problems, the strict body reader, the edge),\napi (the greeting example and the document), server (the binary).\n\nWorkspace lints at the forbid/deny split, the ban list in clippy.toml\nwith generated crate-local scopes, committed .sqlx metadata, the\nOpenAPI document and the error-catalog snapshot, and the tests that\nhold them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2dd3ecb4337751d115732ffa9cde63e703f63ab7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/trees/2dd3ecb4337751d115732ffa9cde63e703f63ab7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/git/commits/ebde085cb3bb780700b6a2554644f088f7df4f99","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commit/ebde085cb3bb780700b6a2554644f088f7df4f99","node_id":"C_kwDOUxcjEdoAKGViZGUwODVjYjNiYjc4MDcwMGI2YTI1NTQ2NDRmMDg4ZjdkZjRmOTk","parents":[],"sha":"ebde085cb3bb780700b6a2554644f088f7df4f99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits/ebde085cb3bb780700b6a2554644f088f7df4f99"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/rust-backend-template/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=5b529364af409c91eb16751e9beba144f5ddb1f4&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T16%3A02%3A36.097Z"}');
